    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-tenure-system-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-ec24463d-a970-4365-a8aa-1f7485ccacc7": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Tenure System",
      "description": "Assistant Professor-Tenure System - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Assistant Professor-Tenure System - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor-Tenure System Linguistics, Languages, And Cultures 10004543 Faculty/Academic Staff Assistant Professor-Tenure System East Lansing, Michigan, United States Linguistics, Languages, And Cultures 10004543 Area of Interest: Education/Training Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Oct 12 2026 Closing at: Oct 12 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Arts And Letters 1173718 Add to favorites View favorites Working/Functional Title Syntax, Assistant Professor-Tenure System Position Summary The Department of Linguistics, Languages and Cultures at Michigan State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Syntax. This is a nine-month, academic year position starting August 16, 2027. Responsibilities include research, teaching, and engagement in institutional and professional service. Candidates must have a PhD in Linguistics or expect to have one by the start of the appointment. They should also have a record of high-quality research in generative syntax and a promising trajectory of scholarly engagement. Preference will be given to candidates whose scholarly interests complement or enhance the existing strengths of the Linguistics faculty. The candidate should demonstrate the potential or proven ability to be an excellent teacher and mentor to graduate and undergraduate students. They will supervise BA and MA theses and doctoral dissertations. The typical teaching load is two courses per semester. The candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate syntax courses, plus other courses in the Linguistics curriculum that align with the candidate's expertise and program needs. They will also contribute as required to the College of Arts and Letters’ general education program in the Integrated Arts and Humanities. This is a union position represented by the Union of Tenure System Faculty (UTSF). The university is working with the union to establish a collective bargaining agreement. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Linguistics Minimum Requirements A PhD in Linguistics or expect to have one at the time of appointment. A record of high-quality research in generative syntax. Strong potential for research likely to result in top-level publications and national recognition. Potential for excellent instruction and mentoring at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Demonstrated ability and/or potential to provide service to the Department, the University, and the profession, and to work with students and faculty from a variety of backgrounds. Desired Qualifications Scholarly interests that complement or enhance the existing strengths of the Linguistics faculty. Required Application Materials Qualified applicants should submit: a cover letter (max 2. pages) current CV a research statement (max. 2 pages) a teaching statement (max. 2 pages) 1 to 3 publications or writing samples representative of your work in your area(s) of expertise the names and email addresses of 3 potential referees (please fill out the initial application with these names and emails) Special Instructions Review of applications will begin November 1 and will continue until the position is filled. Applications must be submitted electronically to the Michigan State University Human Resources website http://careers.msu.edu . Posting number 1173718. For more information, contact Suzanne Wagner, Chair of the Search Committee at wagnersu@msu.edu . Persons with disabilities have the right to request and receive reasonable accommodation. Review of Applications Begins On 11/15/2026 Website lilac.msu.edu MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) eb019cae Last Name (required) 1e1fc235 Email (required) f30ffcac Job Alert 6fd4113d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Linguistics, Languages, And Cultures 10004543 Linguistics, Languages, And Cultures 10004543 Categories Area of Interest: Education/Training Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Area of Interest: Education/Training Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Arts And Letters College Of Arts And Letters By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out the