    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/specialist-advisor-fixed-term-grand-rapids-michigan-united-states-dfdf6401-6f30-48f1-8412-efec7c1e3bca": {
      "title": "Specialist - Advisor-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Specialist - Advisor-Fixed Term - Grand Rapids, Michigan, United States Specialist - Advisor-Fixed Term - Grand Rapids, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Specialist - Advisor-Fixed Term Chm West Michigan 10022803 Faculty/Academic Staff Specialist - Advisor-Fixed Term Grand Rapids, Michigan, United States Chm West Michigan 10022803 Area of Interest: Advising/Counseling Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Health Care Support Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Oct 12 2026 Closing at: Oct 12 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Human Medicine 1173333 Add to favorites View favorites Working/Functional Title Medical Education Learning Specialist Position Summary Michigan State University College of Human Medicine’s Office of Academic Achievement invites applicants for the position of Academic Specialist-Advisor (also known as a Medical Education Learning Specialist). The College of Human Medicine was founded as an innovative educational program embracing new but now widely adopted ideas like community-based education and problem-based learning across eight campuses. Reporting to the Director of Academic Achievement, this position will develop and facilitate programs, services, and resources that support student retention, academic success, and individualized support throughout the Shared Discovery Curriculum. The position is in Grand Rapids, Michigan but may require travel to other sites. The position is remote-friendly. This Academic Specialist-Advisor position is a one-year appointment, renewable annually based on performance and funding availability. As an institution of higher learning, Michigan State University is committed to providing a safe environment for its students, faculty, and staff in support of its educational mission. With this commitment, the University conducts criminal background checks and professional misconduct reviews of all applicants for employment in faculty, academic staff, and executive management searches. Professional Misconduct Review A professional misconduct review is a prerequisite for a candidate to be selected for this position. Applicants will be asked to disclose whether they are subject to any pending investigation, findings or sanctions related to professional misconduct. Professional misconduct includes misconduct related to a person’s employment, including, but not limited to, theft, embezzlement, research integrity, discrimination, or harassment under civil rights laws and policies, including protected identity harassment, sexual harassment, sexual misconduct (sexual assault, sexual exploitation, dating violence, domestic violence, stalking, etc.), and retaliation. All applicants will be asked to sign an authorization and release, which authorizes the University to contact the candidate’s current and former employers, for a period of 7 years prior to the date of application, related to any pending investigations, findings of responsibility and/or sanctions related to professional misconduct. Nothing will be sent to current or former employers unless the candidate reaches the semi-finalist stage. The existence of professional misconduct history does not automatically exclude a candidate from employment. The University will assess the history, including any information provided by the candidate, in determining whether it is compatible with the position. The University may decline to hire a candidate based on the professional misconduct review. All records obtained from external employers will be kept in a secure location, separate from personnel files. If an applicant fails to sign the authorization and release, the application will be deemed incomplete and will be withdrawn. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Masters -Education, Higher Education, Educational Psychology, Sciences, Medical Education, or related fields Desired Degree Doctorate -Education, Teaching, Educational Psychology, Educational Counseling, Sciences, Medical Education, Medicine, or related fields Minimum Requirements Master's degree in Education, Higher Education, Educational Psychology, Sciences, Medical Education, or related fields or equivalent experience Minimum of two years of experience working with diverse adult learners in higher education or medical education settings Familiar with high-impact learning and study strategies Demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion Demonstrated commitment to collaboration with diverse stakeholders Desired Qualifications Doctorate in Education, Teaching, Educational Psychology, Educational Counseling, Sciences, Medical Education, Medicine, or related fields Experience working with students in the medical education or health professions Academic coaching experience Teaching experience Experience administering a tutoring or peer support program Required Application Materials Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (CV) Four References Commitment to the College's Mission and Vision Statement Review of Applications Begins On 10/28/2026 Remote Work Statement MSU strives to provide a flexible work environment and this position has been designated as remote-friendly. Remote-friendly means some or all of the duties can be performed remotely as mutually agreed upon. Website https://humanmedicine.msu.edu/education/academic-achievement.html MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 4339f80a Last Name (required) f823d6fc Email (required) af99562c Job Alert 5dc20ee7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Chm West Michigan 10022803 Chm West Michigan 10022803 Categories Area of Interest: Advising/Counseling Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Health Care Support Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Advising/Counseling Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Health Care Support Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations Grand Rapids, Michigan, United States Grand Rapids, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Human Medicine College Of Human Medicine By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) 8373c79c Last Name (required) 8d8fd9cf Email (required) 35ac1ef4 Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Michigan State University is committed to safeguarding the privacy of personal data. To understand what type of information MSU Sites collects and how that information is used, view the MSU Privacy Statement . Visitors have the option of disabling or not accepting cookies by changing the preferences on their browser. If visitors disable cookies, they will still be able to use most sections of MSU Sites, but some sections may require the use of cookies. MSU also will not be able to tailor content to a visitor’s interests without cookies and a person will not be able to use any parts of MSU Sites that require a login. You consent to our cookies continue to browse this site. If you click on \"Accept essential only\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the My Profile link on the top right of the browser window. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a unit"
