    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-scholar-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-c0f3b9d3-9b8e-4cd0-a118-53846015e73f": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term Teacher Education 10014815 Faculty/Academic Staff Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Teacher Education 10014815 Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Oct 12 2026 Closing at: Oct 12 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Education 1172910 Add to favorites View favorites Working/Functional Title CTP Postdoctoral Scholar Position Summary This Postdoctoral Scholar will work under the supervision of Dr. Noreen Naseem Rodríguez to advance the work of the Creating Transformative Possibility through Asian American Studies (CTP) research team in the final two years of the project. This position offers opportunities to collaborate with dynamic education scholars and contribute to innovative research on Asian American Studies and Ethnic Studies in K-12 schools. Successful candidates will support data collection and analysis, contribute to conference presentations and peer-reviewed publications, and organize team and research events. They will also work closely with faculty, educators, and graduate students as part of a collaborative research team, including established partnerships with researchers at institutions across the nation. This role provides opportunities for scholarly growth, professional development and collaboration, and active engagement in a vibrant research community centered on Asian American Studies in K-12 contexts. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Terminal -Education, Asian American Studies, or Ethnic Studies Minimum Requirements - An earned doctorate in Education, Asian American Studies, or Ethnic Studies is required by the position start date. - Ability to work independently or as a member of a team - Experience working on large-scale research studies - Strong background in education research - Experience publishing peer-reviewed research - Strong organizational and interpersonal skills Desired Qualifications - Specialization in Curriculum and Instruction, Educational Policy, Asian American Studies, and/or Ethnic Studies - Experience conducting qualitative classroom-based research - Strong publication record in peer-reviewed education journals - K-12 teaching experience in the United States (preferably in social studies, English/language arts, and/or ethnic studies) - Strong analytical skills - Strong presentation skills - Attention to detail Required Application Materials Applicants should submit a cover letter, CV, two writing samples and contact information for three references. Candidates should address in their cover letter what draws them to this position, how their scholarship connects to Asian Americans in education, what strengths/skills/experiences they would bring to the research team, and how their previous experiences in education and research make them an ideal candidate for the position. Review of applications will begin on January 4, 2026 until the position is filled. Special Instructions - This is a fully remote position that is funded for twelve months and may be extended an additional year through July 31, 2029. - May have to work on the weekend and/or after business hours. - Site/conference travel as required. Review of Applications Begins On 01/04/2027 Remote Work Statement MSU strives to provide a flexible work environment and this position has been designated as remote-friendly. Remote-friendly means some or all of the duties can be performed remotely as mutually agreed upon. Website education.msu.edu MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) d84c3525 Last Name (required) 0083c7a3 Email (required) 0f5d39ed Job Alert 5cf17a27 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Teacher Education 10014815 Teacher Education 10014815 Categories Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Education College Of Education By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) 0ef65cd0 Last Name (required) b03ce4c1 Email (required) fe23fe2d Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Michigan State University is committed to safeguarding the privacy of personal data. To understand what type of information MSU Sites collects and how that information is used, view the MSU Privacy Statement . Visitors have the option of disabling or not accepting cookies by changing the preferences on their browser. If visitors disable cookies, they will still be able to use most sections of MSU Sites, but some sections may require the use of cookies. MSU also will not be able to tailor content to a visitor’s interests without cookies and a person will not be able to use any parts of MSU Sites that require a login. You consent to our cookies continue to browse this site. If you click on \"Accept essential only\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the My Profile link on the top right of the browser window. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a unit"
