    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-scholar-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-beece170-f3bc-4fd2-9843-d7923a1c82e1": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term Engineering Dean 10016256 Faculty/Academic Staff Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Engineering Dean 10016256 Area of Interest: Engineers/Architects Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Oct 12 2026 Closing at: Oct 12 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Engineering 1172562 Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary Michigan State University (MSU) invites applications from highly motivated candidates with outstanding publication records for multiple joint Postdoctoral Research Associate positions, directly supported by TEMPEST, a new National Science Foundation Science and Technology Center, led by Prof. Michael S. Murillo at MSU: https://tempest-stc.msu.edu The successful candidates will conduct collaborative research at the intersection of non-canonical kinetic theory, non-conventional plasma turbulence modeling, high-speed flows, scientific machine learning for multi-physics problems, agentic multi-modal data science for complex transport phenomena, in addition to forward/backward uncertainty quantification, numerical analysis, and high-performance computing. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Theoretical/computational/experimental physics, engineering, applied/computational mathematics, or a closely related field Minimum Requirements Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in theoretical/computational/experimental physics, engineering, applied/computational mathematics, or a closely related field by the appointment date Desired Qualifications Strong expertise in agentic scientific machine-learning, advanced analysis of fluid mechanics, dusty plasmas, scientific computing, and multi-scale modeling methods are preferred . Required Application Materials Curriculum vitae Cover Letter (At least) Three (3) letters of recommendation Special Instructions Applications will be reviewed upon receipt, and the positions will remain open until filled. Review of Applications Begins On 10/19/2026 Website https://engineering.msu.edu/ MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) c59e0bd2 Last Name (required) 86390521 Email (required) 7bd283c6 Job Alert 7ed442f7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Engineering Dean 10016256 Engineering Dean 10016256 Categories Area of Interest: Engineers/Architects Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Engineers/Architects Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Engineering College Of Enginee