    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-scholar-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-45ca9bf9-659a-45f0-b477-9159d208d8dd": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term Entomology Agriculture And Natural Res 10002268 Faculty/Academic Staff Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Entomology Agriculture And Natural Res 10002268 Area of Interest: Agriculture Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Oct 9 2026 Closing at: Oct 31 2026 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Agriculture And Nat Resources 1172909 Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary The laboratory of Dr. Isaacs in the Department of Entomology at MSU invites applications for a Postdoctoral Scholar position to study Integrated Pest and Pollinator Management, with a focus on developing and testing new management approaches for blueberry production. The position will include field-based research and supporting laboratory research on how different management approaches can support beneficial insects to enhance crop yield and quality. Funding is primarily from a new USDA grant, and the position will connect to ongoing research and extension programs in the laboratory, collaborating with plant pathologists and with MSU Extension pollinator and farm economics programs. This position is well supported by research technicians, a network of university-based staff, and growers working with our lab group. The funding is available for 2+ years, with the initial appointment for 12 months. Annual renewal is expected, based on positive job performance. Our lab group is based in the Department of Entomology within the College of Agriculture and Natural Resources at Michigan State University. MSU is an equal opportunity employer, and we are committed to employee development through creating and sustaining a work environment that values diversity and encourages professional development. We are interested in candidates of all backgrounds who are committed to the principle that academic excellence is achieved through open access and proactive inclusion. As an institution of higher learning, Michigan State University is committed to providing a safe environment for its students, faculty, and staff in support of its educational mission. With this commitment, the University conducts criminal background checks and professional misconduct reviews of all applicants for employment in faculty, academic staff, and executive management searches. A professional misconduct review is a prerequisite for a candidate to be selected for this position. Applicants will be asked to disclose whether they are subject to any pending investigation, findings or sanctions related to professional misconduct. Professional misconduct includes misconduct related to a person’s employment, including, but not limited to, theft, embezzlement, research integrity, discrimination, or harassment under civil rights laws and policies, including protected identity harassment, sexual harassment, sexual misconduct (sexual assault, sexual exploitation, dating violence, domestic violence, stalking, etc.), and retaliation. All applicants will be asked to sign an authorization and release, which authorizes the University to contact the candidate’s current and former employers, for a period of 7 years prior to the date of application, related to any pending investigations, findings of responsibility and/or sanctions related to professional misconduct. Nothing will be sent to current or former employers unless the candidate reaches the semi-finalist stage. The existence of professional misconduct history does not automatically exclude a candidate from employment. The University will assess the history, including any information provided by the candidate, in determining whether it is compatible with the position. The University may decline to hire a candidate based on the professional misconduct review. All records obtained from external employers will be kept in a secure location, separate from personnel files. If an applicant fails to sign the authorization and release, the application will be deemed incomplete and will be withdrawn. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -insect ecology, entomology, biology or similar discipline Minimum Requirements Research experience in entomology, ecology, biological control, pest management, biology or related fields with evidence of a successful publication record, grant writing experience, and ability to work in teams with people from diverse backgrounds. Interest in delivering research-based extension information to fruit growers and beekeepers. Fieldwork will take place across the Lower Peninsula of Michigan, so candidates must possess a valid driver’s license, and be available for intermittent overnight stays. Desired Qualifications Expertise in data analysis and technical writing Experience with entomology fieldwork Project management and logistics Demonstrated capacity to manage people in fieldwork settings Evidence of research publications Experience with on-farm research or extension programs Experience preparing grant proposals Availability to start work during fall 2026 or early 2027 Experience working with fruit crops is desired, but applicants with expertise in pest management, pollinator ecology or management, extension, and/or data analysis in other crop systems are encouraged to apply. Required Application Materials Candidates must submit: 1) a cover letter describing research interests and career goals including a statement of your interest and experience in fostering an inclusive environment, 2) your curriculum vitae, 3) names and contact information for three references, and 4) up to three representative publications. Potential applicants with questions should contact Dr. Isaacs at isaacsr@msu.edu Website www.canr.msu.edu/ent/ MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 3f02f5d7 Last Name (required) 7e63e40d Email (required) a654cae8 Job Alert c5b4aa2a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Entomology Agriculture And Natural Res 10002268 Entomology Agriculture And Natural Res 10002268 Categories Area of Interest: Agriculture Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Agriculture Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Agriculture And Nat Resources College Of Agriculture And Nat Resources By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) 01c225a3 Last Name (required) 15618e00 Email (required) c2500af1 Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Michigan State University is committed to safeguarding the privacy of personal data. To understand what type of information MSU Sites collects and how that information is used, view the MSU Privacy Statement . Visitors have the option of disabling or not accepting cookies by changing the preferences on their browser. If visitors disable cookies, they will still be able to use most sections of MSU Sites, but some sections may require the use of cookies. MSU also will not be able to tailor content to a visitor’s interests without cookies and a person will not be able to use any parts of MSU Sites that require a login. You consent to our cookies continue to browse this site. If you click on \"Accept essential only\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the My Profile link on the top right of the browser window. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a unit"
