    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-full-professor-tenure-system-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-7126e952-22cf-4dfd-8224-9a0e3eafa31b": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Tenure System",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Tenure System - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Tenure System - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Tenure System Mechanical Engineering 10016576 Faculty/Academic Staff Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Tenure System East Lansing, Michigan, United States Mechanical Engineering 10016576 Area of Interest: Engineers/Architects Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Oct 5 2026 Closing at: Oct 5 2028 - 23:55 EDT 100000.00-150000.00 Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Engineering 1171868 Add to favorites View favorites Working/Functional Title Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Tenure System Position Summary The College of Engineering at Michigan State University (MSU) invites applications for a tenure-system faculty position in the Department of Mechanical Engineering (ME). We encourage applications for appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor and will consider exceptional candidates for appointment at the rank of Associate or (Full) Professor. Candidates must have an earned PhD in Mechanical Engineering, or a closely related discipline at the time of appointment, with an anticipated start date of August 16, 2027 . The successful candidate will be expected to develop a sustainable, externally funded, and internationally recognized research program; contribute significantly to their discipline through scholarly work; demonstrate effective teaching and mentorship of both undergraduate and graduate students; and participate in institutional and professional service. Candidates are encouraged to discuss how their research could have an impact and complement the department's existing strengths. All areas of Mechanical Engineering will be considered, with particular interest in: Artificial intelligence (AI)-enhanced/autonomous advanced manufacturing Process engineering, design and optimization assisted by AI Smart materials and medical devices/systems Preference will be given to candidates who can develop a sustainable, externally funded, and internationally recognized research program; contribute significantly to their discipline through scholarly work; demonstrate effective teaching and mentorship of both undergraduate and graduate students; and participate in institutional and professional service. Candidates are encouraged to discuss how their research could impact and complement the strengths within the department. Other qualifications include strong leadership and interpersonal skills, excellent written and oral communication skills, and an ability to work in a collaborative research environment. Joint appointments with other engineering departments are possible, considering existing strengths and capabilities and the candidate’s preferences. Successful candidates will be appointed to an academic-year position in the tenure system, with tenure, if appropriate. Successful candidates are expected to elevate MSU's reputation through their professional activities. This is a union position represented by the Union of Tenure System Faculty (UTSF). The university is working with the union to establish a collective bargaining agreement. Community of Respect and Innovation At Michigan State University’s College of Engineering, we believe that education and innovation are strongest when built on mutual respect. Guided by MSU’s land-grant mission, we are dedicated to advancing knowledge, expanding access to education, and creating solutions that serve the common good. We are committed to a community where each person is respected, supported, and empowered to thrive—engineering with respect, innovating with purpose, building with trust, and growing through resilience. Learn more about our Community of Respect and Innovation . Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Mechanical Engineering or closely related Minimum Requirements Have an earned PhD in Mechanical Engineering, or a closely related discipline at the time of appointment Potential for high-quality instruction and mentoring at the undergraduate and graduate levels Demonstrated ability and/or potential to provide service to the Department, the University, and the profession, and to work with students and faculty from a variety of backgrounds For Assistant Professor candidates: strong potential for high-quality research likely to result in top-level publications and national recognition For Associate/Full Professor candidates: an established national reputation for original and influential research, with demonstrable evidence of continued growth in national status Desired Qualifications Demonstrated leadership ability, with strong interpersonal skills and the capacity to build effective working relationships across diverse teams Excellent written and oral communication skills, with the ability to convey complex information clearly to varied audiences Proven ability to thrive in a collaborative, interdisciplinary research environment Required Application Materials A detailed CV A cover letter summarizing your qualifications A one-page statement of teaching and mentoring philosophy A one-page statement of research philosophy and vision Names and contact information for at least three professional references In your application, please describe the potential impact of your work and how it aligns with the existing strengths of the Department, College, or other programs at MSU. Special Instructions Review of applications will begin on 12/1/2026, and continue until the position is filled. Please direct questions about this position to the search committee chair by email at at chunghas@egr.msu.edu . Review of Applications Begins On 12/01/2026 Website https://engineering.msu.edu/departments/me Department Statement The Department of Mechanical Engineering The Department of Mechanical Engineering currently has the largest student enrollment in the College of Engineering and offers strong interdisciplinary research and educational programs. Its faculty engages in vibrant research across a broad range of areas, including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, combustion, control, design, dynamics, energy and sustainability, fluid dynamics, biomechanics, machine learning, robotics, solid mechanics, and thermal transport. About The College of Engineering For more than 130 years, the MSU College of Engineering has advanced, shared, and applied engineering knowledge to tackle society's most pressing challenges. Guided by MSU's land-grant mission, we prepare exceptional graduates, conduct breakthrough research, and drive innovations that improve lives locally and globally. As an R1 institution, we support our faculty and students with world-class facilities and robust infrastructure for discovery and application, underscored by the college's $87.2 million in annual research expenditures. Our eight departments span computational sciences, energy, health, manufacturing, materials, mobility, security, and sustainability. Through strong collaboration and mentorship, the college provides an environment where faculty can thrive, lead transformative research, and help shape the technologies and solutions of the future. MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 14ed6fcb Last Name (required) 96b47958 Email (required) c325d739 Job Alert b58b4e88 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Mechanical Engineering 10016576 Mechanical Engineering 10016576 Categories Area of Interest: Engineers/Architects Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Area of Interest: Engineers/Architects Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Engineering College Of Engineering By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) 4fd9f20a Last Name (required) 0beca79f Email (required) 3c3b2d04 Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you C