      "title": "Assistant Professor-Tenure System",
      "description": "Assistant Professor-Tenure System - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Assistant Professor-Tenure System - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor-Tenure System Department Of Supply Chain Management 10008570 Faculty/Academic Staff Assistant Professor-Tenure System East Lansing, Michigan, United States Department Of Supply Chain Management 10008570 Area of Interest: Advising/Counseling Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Oct 2 2026 Closing at: Oct 2 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience Eli Broad College Of Business 1171110 Add to favorites View favorites Working/Functional Title Assistant Professor Tenure System Position Summary Michigan State University's Eli Broad College of Business, Department of Supply Chain Management, has an opening for a tenure system assistant professor in Operations Management and Supply Chain Management to start in the 2027-2028 academic year. Duties include research, teaching, and service, and the teaching responsibility would involve Supply Chain or related courses. Please note that this is a union position represented by the Union of Tenure System Faculty (UTSF). The university is working with the union to establish a collective bargaining agreement. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Supply Chain Management, Operations Management or related field Minimum Requirements The position requires a Ph.D. or equivalent degree from an accredited university. Candidates must have a conferred Ph.D. in Supply Chain Management or related field as of the start date of the position, and have a demonstrated record of research excellence, commensurate with their rank. Desired Qualifications Preference for candidates whose research focuses on healthcare operations and/or sustainability. Connections to risk and resilience within these supply chains would also be encouraged. Consistent with the language used in our previous search, we would welcome candidates using a range of empirical approaches, including data science, machine learning, and empirical analytics. Required Application Materials CV and Cover Letter Special Instructions Review of applications will begin as early as October 2026, and continue until the position is filled. To ensure full consideration, applications should be received by November 10th, 2026. Applications must be submitted online at: http://careers.msu.edu Please reach out to Dr. Shawnee Vickery @ vickery@broad.msu.edu with any questions about the position. Review of Applications Begins On 10/10/2026 Remote Work Statement MSU strives to provide a flexible work environment and this position has been designated as remote-friendly. Remote-friendly means some or all of the duties can be performed remotely as mutually agreed upon. Website https://broad.msu.edu/supply-chain-management/ Department Statement Highly ranked in US News and World Report, the Supply Chain Management Department ( https://broad.msu.edu/supply-chain-management/) is the home of internationally recognized faculty who are among the most accomplished scholars and teachers. The department offers a Bachelors degree in Supply Chain Management, a graduate certificate in Elements of Global Supply Chain Management, an MS in Supply Chain Management, and Ph.Ds in both Logistics Management, and Operations & Sourcing Management. The department contributes heavily to the Executive and Full-time MBA programs, online certificate programs, and is very active in executive education programs. MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 1fd9b33c Last Name (required) 9c2a4cd7 Email (required) c3ecd070 Job Alert a5d26f4b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Department Of Supply Chain Management 10008570 Department Of Supply Chain Management 10008570 Categories Area of Interest: Advising/Counseling Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Advising/Counseling Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit Eli Broad College Of Business Eli Broad College Of Business By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles th