    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/specialist-advisor-continuing-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-cf048174-ce81-47e3-9b14-9d7d7cf67008": {
      "title": "Specialist - Advisor-Continuing",
      "description": "Specialist - Advisor-Continuing - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Specialist - Advisor-Continuing - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Specialist - Advisor-Continuing Natural Science Dean 10032604 Faculty/Academic Staff Specialist - Advisor-Continuing East Lansing, Michigan, United States Natural Science Dean 10032604 Area of Interest: Advising/Counseling Area of Interest: Student Services/Student Affairs Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Continuing System Academic Staff Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Oct 2 2026 Closing at: Oct 2 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Natural Science 1172086 Add to favorites View favorites Working/Functional Title Student Success Advisor - NatSci Position Summary The College of Natural Science at Michigan State University welcomes applications for a Student Success Advisor position within the Undergraduate Academic and Student Affairs Office. This twelve-month, continuing system Academic Specialist position offers an opportunity to make a meaningful impact on student success through advising, coaching, and proactive student support initiatives. The selected individual will report to the Director of Academic Advising and Student Success Initiatives. The Student Success Advisor will collaborate with the Student Success Team to develop and implement proactive student success initiatives that support undergraduate student retention, academic achievement, and overall well-being. Duties include student success advising, assisting with Academic Standing of Undergraduate Students (ASUS) Day, representing the college on various campus committees, making referrals to campus resources, and providing life coaching meetings for students. The Student Success Advisor supports the mission of the Undergraduate Academic and Student Affairs Office by providing individualized student support and contributing to the development of programs and initiatives that promote academic success. The Advisor will be expected to fulfill the following responsibilities: Hold Student Success Advising appointments (e.g., time management, study skills, test-taking strategies) Manage a caseload of UGRD 10 and UGRD 20 students on academic probation Provide life coaching meetings Maintain accurate records and documentation of student interaction. Participate in College and University events, including but not limited to Colloquium, Commencement, and Admitted Students Day. Communicate effectively with various audiences using email, social media, video conferencing software, small group, and individual sessions as appropriate. Continuously develop knowledge of best practices, policies and procedures, and technological tools related to academic advising. Collaborate on building proactive student success initiatives Assist with the Academic Standing of Undergraduate Students process each semester Represent the college on various campus-wide committees. Collect data and use it to inform the building of student success resources. The successful candidate will have demonstrated: Ability to establish and maintain rapport when working with students and colleagues. An understanding of science curricula or experience working with STEM students Ability to adapt to change and critically think through complex situations. Strong interpersonal skills. Demonstrated ability and willingness to work both autonomously and as a key member of a collaborative team. Evidence of and commitment to professional development Excellent communication skills to communicate effectively and credibly, both verbally and in writing, with all audiences. Ability to work independently while functioning as part of a team. Ability to use new and existing technologies to manage data and communicate with students, including working knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite. Excellent communication skills to communicate effectively and credibly, both verbally and in writing, with all audiences. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Masters -Education/higher education, student affairs, counseling, the sciences, or other relevant field Minimum Requirements Master’s degree in education/higher education, student affairs, counseling, the sciences, or other relevant field. Evidence of successful collaborations around issues related to advising and student success. Desired Qualifications Experience working in a college academic setting preferred. Academic advising experience preferred. Required Application Materials Complete applications must include: 1) a cover letter summarizing qualifications for the position 2) curriculum vitae/resume 3) a statement of the candidate's advising philosophy (one-page maximum) 4) contact information for 3 references Complete applications must be received preferably by October 14, 2026 to receive full consideration. Late submissions will be considered if suitable candidates are not identified by the deadline. Review of Applications Begins On 10/14/2026 Remote Work Statement MSU strives to provide a flexible work environment and this position has been designated as remote-friendly. Remote-friendly means some or all of the duties can be performed remotely as mutually agreed upon. Website natsci.msu.edu MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) da41df0d Last Name (required) 75f71884 Email (required) 3dd2df95 Job Alert 6dc7fce6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Natural Science Dean 10032604 Natural Science Dean 10032604 Categories Area of Interest: Advising/Counseling Area of Interest: Student Services/Student Affairs Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Continuing System Academic Staff Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Advising/Counseling Area of Interest: Student Services/Student Affairs Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Continuing System Academic Staff Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Natural Science College Of Natural Science By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) 0cf69d51 Last Name (required) 55d4a3b4 Email (required) 871ec95a Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Michigan State University is committed to safeguarding the privacy of personal data. To understand what type of information MSU Sites collects and how that information is used, view the MSU Privacy Statement . Visitors have the option of disabling or not accepting cookies by changing the preferences on their browser. If visitors disable cookies, they will still be able to use most sections of MSU Sites, but some sections may require the use of cookies. MSU also will not be able to tailor content to a visitor’s interests without cookies and a person will not be able to use any parts of MSU Sites that require a login. You consent to our cookies continue to browse this site. If you click on \"Accept essential only\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the My Profile link on the top right of the browser window. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a unit"
