      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term Biochemistry & Molecular Biology Cns 10032098 Faculty/Academic Staff Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Biochemistry & Molecular Biology Cns 10032098 Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Oct 1 2026 Closing at: Oct 1 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Natural Science 1171367 Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary Postdoctoral scholars are sought to carry out computational research on biophysical questions in the Feig lab. Research topics will focus on biomolecular condensates, crowded cellular environments, and, more generally, exploration of the sequence-structure-dynamics-function relationships of biomolecules in cellular environments. Research will involve a range of computational techniques, including classical molecular simulations at different levels of resolution and the development and application of neural network models, including generative modeling approaches. Candidates are expected to conduct research independently, apply and develop advanced computational methods, communicate findings internally at regular intervals, disseminate results externally through peer-reviewed publications and conference presentations, collaborate with other group members as appropriate, and assume mentoring responsibilities for junior lab members. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Chemistry, Biochemistry, Physics, Computational Science or closely related field. Minimum Requirements Research experience applying computational methods to biological systems Proficiency in Python programming Excellent written and verbal communication skills First-author peer-reviewed publication(s) Desired Qualifications Experience conducting and analyzing molecular dynamics simulations Experience using high-performance computing platforms Experience developing neural network models Experience using AI-assisted coding tools for software development Experience working in interdisciplinary teams, including collaborations with experimentalists Required Application Materials CV Special Instructions This is initially a one-year assignment, possibly longer, with possible renewal contingent upon satisfactory review and funding. Review of Applications Begins On 10/12/2026 Remote Work Statement MSU strives to provide a flexible work environment and this position has been designated as remote-friendly. Remote-friendly means some or all of the duties can be performed remotely as mutually agreed upon. Website https://feiglab.org/ MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) e530a562 Last Name (required) 3bd0183b Email (required) aa0c4e1a Job Alert 8b62dfdf Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your