    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-full-professor-tenure-system-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-637ab15c-cf93-46ee-a4c2-468abfec22b0": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Tenure System",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Tenure System - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Tenure System - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Tenure System Department Of Marketing 10008877 Faculty/Academic Staff Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Tenure System East Lansing, Michigan, United States Department Of Marketing 10008877 Area of Interest: Education/Training Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Sep 30 2026 Closing at: Sep 30 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience Eli Broad College Of Business 1170112 Add to favorites View favorites Working/Functional Title Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Tenure System Position Summary The Marketing Department at the Broad College of Business, Michigan State University, seeks applications for an assistant, associate or full professor to begin in the Fall of 2027. We encourage applications from excellent candidates in all research areas. Candidates at the assistant, associate or full professor levels must have a Ph.D. in marketing or related areas and have a record of high-quality, top-tier publications and demonstrated teaching excellence. Applicants must show continued research productivity and achievement of scholarly prominence and be willing to work with doctoral students and other faculty members. All applicants should demonstrate ability as a classroom instructor through summarized peer and/or student evaluations and/or explicit commentary in letters of recommendation. The department’s Ph.D., M.S., M.B.A., and B.A. programs are highly regarded (see https://broad.msu.edu/marketing/ ). While candidates with expertise in all areas of specialization will be considered, we especially seek scholars with expertise in marketing strategy, empirical modeling, international business/marketing, and/or sales who can contribute to the excellence of our current faculty. Please note that this is a union position represented by the Union of Tenure System Faculty (UTSF). The university is working with the union to establish a collective bargaining agreement. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Terminal -Marketing or related Minimum Requirements Candidates at the assistant, associate or full professor levels must have a Ph.D. in marketing or related areas and have a record of high-quality, top-tier publications and demonstrated teaching excellence. Required Application Materials Applicants must submit a statement addressing how they would contribute to the mission of the Department and the Broad College of Business through their research, teaching, and/or service, including how the applicant would contribute to the Department’s commitment to being an inclusive educational and working environment for the students, faculty, staff, and other stakeholders of the Broad College of Business. This statement should be submitted along with the cover letter, CV, teaching evaluations, letters of recommendation, and other requested materials. Special Instructions For more information, please contact Dr. Forrest Morgeson, Chair of the Search Committee at morgeso3@broad.msu.edu). Review of Applications Begins On 12/01/2026 Remote Work Statement MSU strives to provide a flexible work environment and this position has been designated as remote-friendly. Remote-friendly means some or all of the duties can be performed remotely as mutually agreed upon. Website https://broad.msu.edu/marketing/ MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) ee06c06b Last Name (required) e0342127 Email (required) 015b5008 Job Alert fd20b607 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Department Of Marketing 10008877 Department Of Marketing 10008877 Categories Area of Interest: Education/Training Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Education/Training Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit Eli Broad College Of Business Eli Broad College Of Business By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) a99f7777 Last Name (required) bd53460c Email (required) c45bec35 Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you ac