    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/ast-prof-asc-prof-prof-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-62ad1750-b099-4e91-ae21-544afc4f649d": {
      "title": "Ast Prof/Asc Prof/Prof Fixed Term",
      "description": "Ast Prof/Asc Prof/Prof Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Ast Prof/Asc Prof/Prof Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Ast Prof/Asc Prof/Prof Fixed Term Computer Science And Engineering 10016172 Faculty/Academic Staff Ast Prof/Asc Prof/Prof Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Computer Science And Engineering 10016172 Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Information Technology Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Sep 28 2026 Closing at: Sep 27 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Engineering 1171186 Add to favorites View favorites Working/Functional Title Ast Prof/Asc Prof/Prof Fixed Term Position Summary The College of Engineering at Michigan State University (MSU) invites applications for a fixed-term faculty position in the Department of Computer Science and Engineering (CSE). Applications will be considered at all ranks (Assistant, Associate, and Full Professor), with particular interest in candidates who bring several years of relevant experience. This is an annual (12-month), end-dated position that may be renewed annually. The position is anticipated to continue for five years, with the potential to transition to a tenure-system position following the five-year period. Continued employment and annual renewal depend on satisfactory performance, continued funding availability, and mutual agreement between the faculty member and the College of Engineering. Candidates must have an earned PhD in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a closely related discipline at the time of appointment, with an anticipated start date of August 16, 2027 . The successful candidate will be expected to develop a sustainable, externally funded, and internationally recognized research program; contribute significantly to their discipline through scholarly work; demonstrate effective teaching and mentorship of both undergraduate and graduate students; and participate in institutional and professional service. Candidates are encouraged to discuss how their research could have an impact and complement the department's existing strengths. Other qualifications include strong leadership and interpersonal skills, excellent written and oral communication skills, and an ability to work in a collaborative research environment. Joint appointments with other engineering departments are possible, considering existing strengths and capabilities and the candidate’s preferences. Successful candidates are expected to elevate MSU's reputation through their professional activities. Target Area: AI and Cybersecurity The target area encompasses two complementary themes, and we seek applicants with expertise in one or both: 1) security of AI and 2) AI for security. Security of AI focuses on protecting AI systems, data, models, and users from adversarial attacks and unintended behavior, including data poisoning, prompt injection, model theft, privacy leakage, and unsafe outputs. Approaches include secure data practices, robust training, runtime monitoring, access control, formal verification, and verification-aware programming languages. It also includes ensuring that increasingly capable and autonomous AI agents remain aligned with their intended objectives and operational constraints and do not exhibit unintended, deceptive, or harmful behavior. AI for security advances cybersecurity through AI-driven vulnerability discovery, malware analysis, intrusion detection, fraud prevention, threat intelligence, and automated response. These methods enable the analysis of large-scale security data and the detection of emerging threats. Together, these directions aim to make AI systems more trustworthy and resilient while making cybersecurity more adaptive, scalable, and proactive. Community of Respect and Innovation At Michigan State University’s College of Engineering, we believe that education and innovation are strongest when built on mutual respect. Guided by MSU’s land-grant mission, we are dedicated to advancing knowledge, expanding access to education, and creating solutions that serve the common good. We are committed to a community where each person is respected, supported, and empowered to thrive—engineering with respect, innovating with purpose, building with trust, and growing through resilience. Learn more about our Community of Respect and Innovation . Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -PhD in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a closely related discipline. Minimum Requirements Have an earned PhD in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a closely related discipline at the time of appointment. Potential for high-quality instruction and mentoring at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Demonstrated ability and/or potential to provide service to the Department, the University, and the profession, and to work with students and faculty from a variety of backgrounds. For Assistant Professor candidates: strong potential for high-quality research likely to result in top-level publications and national recognition. For Associate/Full Professor candidates: an established national reputation for original and influential research, with demonstrable evidence of continued growth in national status. Desired Qualifications Demonstrated leadership ability, with strong interpersonal skills and the capacity to build effective working relationships across diverse teams. Excellent written and oral communication skills, with the ability to convey complex information clearly to varied audiences. Proven ability to thrive in a collaborative, interdisciplinary research environment. Required Application Materials A detailed CV. A cover letter summarizing your qualifications. A one-page statement of teaching and mentoring philosophy. A one-page statement of research philosophy and vision. Names and contact information for at least three professional references. In your application, please describe the potential impact of your work and how it aligns with the existing strengths of the Department, College, or other programs at MSU. Special Instructions Review of applications will begin on December 1, 2026 , and continue until the position is filled. Please direct questions about this position to the search committee chair, Prof. Borzoo Bonakdarpour, by email at faculty-search-chair@cse.msu.edu . Review of Applications Begins On 12/01/2026 Website https://engineering.msu.edu/departments/cse Department Statement The Department of Computer Science and Engineering has robust research programs spanning artificial intelligence, autonomous driving, biometrics, computer vision, cybersecurity and privacy, data science, evolutionary computation, machine learning, networking, formal methods, and software engineering. The Department is home to 55 tenure-system faculty members and teaching specialists, including four endowed professors, 13 NSF CAREER Award recipients, and one member of the National Academy of Engineering, with annual research expenditures exceeding $11 million. The Department offers accredited B.S. degree programs in Computer Science and Computer Engineering, as well as a B.S. degree in Computational Data Science. Graduate programs include M.S. and Ph.D. degrees in Computer Science and an interdisciplinary M.S. degree in Data Science offered in collaboration with the Department of Statistics and the Department of Computational Mathematics, Science and Engineering. For additional information about the CSE Department, please visit https://cse.msu.edu/ . About The College of Engineering For more than 130 years, the MSU College of Engineering has advanced, shared, and applied engineering knowledge to tackle society's most pressing challenges. Guided by MSU's land-grant mission, we prepare exceptional graduates, conduct breakthrough research, and drive innovations that improve lives locally and globally. As an R1 institution, we support our faculty and students with world-class facilities and robust infrastructure for discovery and application, underscored by the college's $71 million in annual research expenditures. Our eight departments span computational sciences, energy, health, manufacturing, materials, mobility, security, and sustainability. Through strong collaboration and mentorship, the college provides an environment where faculty can thrive, lead transformative research, and help shape the technologies and solutions of the future. MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) a21d6a80 Last Name (required) 2289ef9a Email (required) 3318856d Job Alert d34a0c47 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Computer Science And Engineering 10016172 Computer Science And Engineering 10016172 Categories Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Information Technology Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Union Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Information Technology Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Engineering College Of Engineering By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) c1a68086 Last Name (required) c614b807 Email (required) c29cecd5 Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Michigan State University is committed to safeguarding the privacy of personal data. To understand what type of information MSU Sites collects and how that information is used, view the MSU Privacy Statement . Visitors have the option of disabling or not accepting cookies by changing the preferences on their browser. If visitors disable cookies, they will still be able to use most sections of MSU Sites, but some sections may require