    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/specialist-advisor-continuing-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-516831cc-1e61-4a09-8853-3fa832331c5d": {
      "title": "Specialist - Advisor-Continuing",
      "description": "Specialist - Advisor-Continuing - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Specialist - Advisor-Continuing - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Specialist - Advisor-Continuing Broad Undergraduate Academic Services 40001144 Faculty/Academic Staff Specialist - Advisor-Continuing East Lansing, Michigan, United States Broad Undergraduate Academic Services 40001144 Area of Interest: Advising/Counseling Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Continuing System Academic Staff Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Sep 28 2026 Closing at: Sep 28 2028 - 23:55 EDT 60389.00-87000.00 Salary Commensurate with Experience Eli Broad College Of Business 1170933 Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary The Assistant Director for Global Support Services provides leadership for the academic advising and support services that contribute to the global experiences of undergraduate students within the Eli Broad College of Business. The position serves as the primary Undergraduate Academic Services (UAS) resource for matters related to international students, incoming exchange students, and Broad students participating in education abroad programs. The Assistant Director leads the development, coordination, and continuous improvement of advising practices, processes, resources, and staff training related to global student support. This includes helping students navigate the intersection of Broad College academic requirements and international educational experiences; coordinating academic support for incoming exchange students and students participating in semester, summer, faculty-directed, exchange, and other education abroad programs; leading the administration and student communication for the Broad International Business minor; identifying and addressing barriers affecting globally engaged students; and partnering with College and University colleagues to support effective and consistent services. As a member of the UAS Admin Team, the Assistant Director contributes to unit leadership, planning, and decision-making and supervises approximately 2-3 professional academic advisors. Supervisory responsibilities include coaching and professional development, performance management, workload planning, and providing guidance on complex advising and student-support matters. The Assistant Director also provides leadership and training to the broader UAS team in areas related to global programs, policies, procedures, and academic planning. The Assistant Director maintains an academic advising caseload and provides comprehensive advising to prospective students, business-preference students, and admitted Broad students. Advising may include degree and course planning, major and career pathway exploration, education abroad planning, interpretation of academic policies and requirements, graduation planning, and connection to appropriate College and University resources. The position serves as a resource to students and colleagues when academic situations involve international coursework, exchange programs, education abroad, or other complex academic considerations. The position also contributes to broader UAS efforts supporting student success, persistence, and degree completion, including prospective and new student programming, student outreach and interventions, degree clearance, College events, and other student-facing initiatives. The Assistant Director teaches sessions supporting the semester education abroad pre-departure course each fall and spring and may facilitate a one-credit seminar emphasizing first year experience or senior launch. The position represents UAS through appropriate College and University committees, partnerships, and initiatives and works regularly with faculty, academic professionals, and administrative colleagues across the University. UAS supports flexible work arrangements that may include predictable day/time flexibility and remote work opportunities, consistent with university policy, operational needs, and student-facing responsibilities. More than 50% of this position’s responsibilities require on-site work. Flexible schedules are coordinated within the team each semester and are expected to be predictable, reliable, and supportive of continuity of service. Occasional evening or weekend work may be required to support events, student-facing activities, or university initiatives. The minimum salary for this position is $77,000. Final salary will be commensurate with relevant experience, educational credentials, position scope, and internal equity. Every effort will be made to provide a competitive salary that is equitable among Broad undergraduate-facing professionals. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Masters -Education, counseling, student affairs, higher education, business, international education, or a related field. Minimum Requirements Well-prepared candidates will demonstrate: A minimum of five years of progressively responsible experience supporting undergraduate students through academic advising or comparable student services. Demonstrated professional experience directly supporting international students, incoming exchange students, education abroad participants, or comparable globally engaged student populations, including academic planning and the interpretation or application of related academic policies and requirements. Demonstrated experience leading or coordinating an area of student services, advising operations, or a comparable functional portfolio, including responsibility for developing or improving processes, practices, resources, or service delivery. Experience supervising professional staff, including providing ongoing direction, coaching, feedback, and performance management. Demonstrated ability to interpret and apply academic policies, procedures, and requirements and exercise sound judgment in complex student situations. Experience coordinating programs, services, projects, or processes involving multiple stakeholders. Strong written, verbal, interpersonal, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with students and colleagues from a wide range of backgrounds and experiences. Desired Qualifications Experience providing academic support to both incoming international or exchange students and students participating in education abroad. Experience supporting the academic planning and administration of semester-long education abroad or exchange programs. Knowledge of academic issues associated with international coursework, education abroad, transfer credit, degree applicability, course sequencing, student progression, and graduation planning. Experience developing and implementing advising procedures, staff training, communication resources, or service-delivery standards related to international or education abroad student support. Experience providing leadership within an academic advising, international education, education abroad, or undergraduate student services unit. Experience using student information systems, advising technologies, reporting tools, and customer relationship management systems. Experience using data, assessment, or student feedback to evaluate and improve programs and services. Facilitation, presentation, or teaching experience in a college or university setting. Required Application Materials Resume Cover letter Contact information of three professional references Review of Applications Begins On 10/07/2026 Remote Work Statement MSU strives to provide a flexible work environment and this position has been designated as remote-friendly. Remote-friendly means some or all of the duties can be performed remotely as mutually agreed upon. Website https://broad.msu.edu/undergraduate/ MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 1431ed57 Last Name (required) e09abe41 Email (required) cc204cbf Job Alert 50d99a3d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Broad Undergraduate Academic Services 40001144 Broad Undergraduate Academic Services 40001144 Categories Area of Interest: Advising/Counseling Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Continuing System Academic Staff Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Advising/Counseling Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Continuing System Academic Staff Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit Eli Broad College Of Business Eli Broad College Of Business By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) 5b42223c Last Name (required) 7c20c8bb Email (required) d91e0961 Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Michigan State University is committed to safeguarding the privacy of personal data. To understand what type of information MSU Sites collects and how that information is used, view the MSU Privacy Statement . Visitors have the option of disabling or not accepting cookies by changing the preferences on their browser. If visitors disable cookies, they will still be able to use most sections of MSU Sites, but some sections may require the use of cookies. MSU also will not be able to tailor content to a visitor’s interests without cookies and a person will not be able to use any parts of MSU Sites that require a login. You consent to our cookies continue to browse this site. If you click on \"Accept essential only\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the My Profile link on the top right of the browser window. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a unit"
