    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-scholar-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-27461a60-51aa-4389-bb0f-7020fe974184": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term Computational Math Sci And Engr Cns 40000838 Faculty/Academic Staff Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Computational Math Sci And Engr Cns 40000838 Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Sep 28 2026 Closing at: Sep 28 2028 - 23:55 EDT 60000.00-65000.00 Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Natural Science 1169918 Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary The successful candidate will work with Dr. Kunlun Qi < https://kunlun-qi.github.io > on research projects related to kinetic equation and its related multiscale model reduction, numerical method, and data-driven/machine-learning approaches, including: · Numerical simulation of kinetic equations: fast algorithms with stability/convergence analysis; · Data-driven and machine learning-assisted methods: data assimilation, uncertainty quantification (UQ), and machine-learning-based moment closure models. · Multiscale modeling: kinetic limits of many-particle dynamical systems, hydrodynamic limits of kinetic models, and semiclassical limits of quantum systems. · Theoretical analysis for kinetic PDEs: Well-posedness and asymptotic behavior of the Boltzmann equation and related models Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Terminal -Ph.D. in Mathematics, Statistics, or a closely related field by the start of the appointment. Minimum Requirements Ph.D. in Mathematics, Statistics, or a closely related field by the start of the appointment. Desired Qualifications Candidates with strong backgrounds in kinetic equation, numerical analysis, scientific computing, PDE together with research experience in scientific machine learning, are particularly encouraged to apply. Required Application Materials Applications will be reviewed immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should submit: ·A curriculum vitae; · A research statement describing prior and current research, future research plans, and specific interests related to the project; · At least two letters of recommendation. Special Instructions Prospective candidates are welcome to contact Dr. Kunlun Qi at qikunlun@msu.edu. Please include “Postdoc Applicant – Your name” in the subject line and briefly describe any overlap between your research interests and the topics of the position. Applications and all supporting materials must be submitted electronically through MathJobs. If you are perspective graduate students who are interested in our research, we are also looking for self-motivated Master/PhD joining our group, please see more details in our graduate program and contact Dr. Kunlun Qi at qikunlun@msu.edu Review of Applications Begins On 10/14/2026 Website https://cmse.msu.edu/ Department Statement Michigan State University (MSU) is one of the top public research universities in the United States, located in the scenic city of East Lansing, Michigan. MSU boasts world-class research capabilities, a diverse and inclusive campus culture, and abundant academic resources. It has a strong academic reputation in applied mathematics, computational science, and mathematical physics—making it an ideal place for academic development and research exploration. The Department of Computational Mathematics, Science and Engineering (CMSE) was founded in 2015 as an interdisciplinary department jointly administered by the College of Natural Science and the College of Engineering. CMSE centers around computational approaches, encompassing algorithm development, high-performance computing, scientific modeling, and data science. The department has an active research community with strengths in computational biology, bioinformatics, machine learning, optimization, scientific computing, statistical data analysis, and topological data analysis. CMSE offers undergraduate, master’s, and Ph.D. programs in data science, emphasizing both research and teaching to support student growth. MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 4ae5784d Last Name (required) ba7bf0d0 Email (required) b5f150ce Job Alert 48ed93df Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Computational Math Sci And Engr Cns 40000838 Computational Math Sci And Engr Cns 40000838 Categories Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Natural Science College Of Natural Science By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) 40f6812e Last Name (required) 1d8eec9c Email (required) 4dfe5657 Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Michigan State University is committed to safeguarding the privacy of personal data. To understand what type of information MSU Sites collects and how that information is used, view the MSU Privacy Statement . Visitors have the option of disabling or not accepting cookies by changing the preferences on their browser. If visitors disable cookies, they will still be able to use most sections of MSU Sites, but some sections may require the use of cookies. MSU also will not be able to tailor content to a visitor’s interests without cookies and a person will not be able to use any parts of MSU Sites that require a login. You consent to our cookies continue to browse this site. If you click on \"Accept essential only\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the My Profile link on the top right of the browser window. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a unit"
