    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-scholar-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-4ee8df41-2cad-47fd-ac50-24011a980658": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term Biochemistry & Molecular Biology Cns 10032098 Faculty/Academic Staff Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Biochemistry & Molecular Biology Cns 10032098 Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Sep 28 2026 Closing at: Sep 28 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Natural Science 1169875 Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary A postdoctoral position is available in the laboratory of Dr. Kristin N. Parent at Michigan State University. The Parent lab’s research focuses on a correlated approach to deciphering the processes of virus assembly and infection via a combination of biochemistry, molecular biology, biophysics, structural biology, and experimental evolution studies. The main project of the laboratory involves understanding host-recognition mechanisms in dsDNA-containing bacteriophage. Applications will be considered from highly motivated individuals with a Ph.D. degree in the Natural Sciences. Preference will be given to applicants with demonstrated expertise in the following: structural biology methods ( e.g. cryo-electron microscopy), molecular biology expertise, bacterial genetics or virus-related research, general knowledge of biochemistry techniques (including but not limited to gel electrophoresis, sterile techniques, plating protocols, and general microbiology). Applicants with mammalian cell culture experience are also encouraged to apply. Specific duties for this position include: Performing tests and assays to generate data for research (focused ion beam milling, cryo-electron tomography of phage infected cells or similar, image analysis and three dimensional reconstructions). (75% of time) Writing manuscripts (5% of time) Professional development (10% of time) General lab duties including but not limited to shared chores, attendance at group meetings or other lab events, etc. (10% of time) This work was supported in part by the MSU Research Foundation Postdoctoral Scholars Program, Office of Research and Innovation, Michigan State University. This program is aligned with the research priorities of the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services (HHS). Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Natural Sciences Minimum Requirements Ph.D. degree in the Natural Sciences Evidence of productivity via publications Desired Qualifications Preference will be given to applicants with demonstrated expertise in the following: structural biology methods ( e.g. cryo-electron microscopy), molecular biology expertise, bacterial genetics or virus-related research, general knowledge of biochemistry techniques (including but not limited to gel electrophoresis, sterile techniques, plating protocols, and general microbiology). Applicants with mammalian cell culture experience are also encouraged to apply. Required Application Materials cover letter CV names and contact information for 2-3 letter writers Special Instructions Must be available to start before 2/15/2027. Review of Applications Begins On 10/05/2026 Website https://kparentlab.natsci.msu.edu/ MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) e0e881fc Last Name (required) b614a3e3 Email (required) 2a1cda44 Job Alert 0fee22f1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Biochemistry & Molecular Biology Cns 10032098 Biochemistry & Molecular Biology Cns 10032098 Categories Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Natural Science College Of Natural Science By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Profess