    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-scholar-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-47b694a1-1655-47bc-a9c9-54eaf4fb0d5a": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term Mathematics 10032574 Faculty/Academic Staff Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Mathematics 10032574 Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Sep 21 2026 Closing at: Sep 21 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Natural Science 1166718 Add to favorites View favorites Working/Functional Title Departmental Postdocs/Research Associates Position Summary The Department of Mathematics at Michigan State University invites applications for Postdoctoral Scholars with a starting date of Fall 2027. Postdoctoral scholar positions fall into two categories: Departmental Postdocs or Grant-funded Postdocs. Departmental Postdocs comprise the department Postdoctoral Fellows program. Postdoctoral Fellows contribute to the research and instructional mission of our unit. These are academic year appointed positions. Grant-funded Postdocs support the research activities of currently funded external research grants, as outlined in the grants statement of work and budget. These positions are either academic or annual year appointments. All positions are benefits eligible and potentially renewable on an annual basis through Spring 2030, contingent upon satisfactory performance and availability of funding. Candidates will be evaluated on their potential in research and teaching. Candidates are required to have a Ph.D. in Mathematics or related field by August 10, 2027. Applications from all areas of mathematical research will be considered. Postdoctoral scholars will be paired with faculty mentors with whom they have compatible research interests and will engage in our active instructional mentoring program. Applicants should submit a curriculum vitae, statements on research and on teaching, and arrange for at least four (4) letters of recommendation to be submitted, one of which must specifically address the applicant's teaching experiences. It is helpful if the cover letter indicates if the applicant wishes to be considered by specific MSU faculty. Applications must be submitted via mathjobs.org . Submit your application directly at https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/28828 . The evaluation process will begin on December 1, 2026, and review of applications will continue until positions are filled. A background check is required for employment. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Mathematics or related field Minimum Requirements Candidates are required to have a Ph.D. in Mathematics or related field by August 10, 2027. Applications from all areas of mathematical research will be considered. Postdoctoral scholars will be paired with faculty mentors with whom they have compatible research interests and will engage in our active instructional mentoring program. Applicants should submit a curriculum vitae, statements on research and on teaching, and arrange for at least four (4) letters of recommendation to be submitted, one of which must specifically address the applicant's teaching experiences. It is helpful if the cover letter indicates if the applicant wishes to be considered by specific MSU faculty. Required Application Materials Candidates are required to have a Ph.D. in Mathematics or related field by August 10, 2027. Applications from all areas of mathematical research will be considered. Postdoctoral scholars will be paired with faculty mentors with whom they have compatible research interests and will engage in our active instructional mentoring program. Applicants should submit a curriculum vitae, statements on research and on teaching, and arrange for at least four (4) letters of recommendation to be submitted, one of which must specifically address the applicant's teaching experiences. It is helpful if the cover letter indicates if the applicant wishes to be considered by specific MSU faculty. Applications must be submitted via mathjobs.org . Submit your application directly at https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/28828 . Special Instructions Applications must be submitted via mathjobs.org . Submit your application directly at https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/28828 . T he evaluation process will begin on December 1, 2026, and review of applications will continue until positions are filled. A background check is required for employment. Review of Applications Begins On 12/01/2026 Website https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/28828 Department Statement The Department of Mathematics strives for world-class excellence in core research, innovation in instruction in a time of evolving student needs, and engagement with strategic initiatives with our sister units to push the frontiers of science. MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) e3107f09 Last Name (required) 48148524 Email (required) 411ea343 Job Alert 378bd4c2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Mathematics 10032574 Mathematics 10032574 Categories Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Natural Science College Of Natural Science By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a