      "title": "Director I-Fixed-Acad Staff",
      "description": "Director I-Fixed-Acad Staff - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Director I-Fixed-Acad Staff - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Director I-Fixed-Acad Staff Intercollegiate Athletics 10070478 Faculty/Academic Staff Director I-Fixed-Acad Staff East Lansing, Michigan, United States Intercollegiate Athletics 10070478 Area of Interest: Athletics/Recreation Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Sep 21 2026 Closing at: Sep 21 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience Intercollegiate Athletics 1169583 Add to favorites View favorites Working/Functional Title Deputy Athletics Director, Chief Operating Officer Position Summary MSU Athletics is searching for a Deputy Athletics Director to provide day-to-day executive leadership for Michigan State Athletics and represent the Director of Athletics on University, conference, and external matters. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Serve as the CEO of Spartan Ventures to implement strategic priorities, increase revenue, and optimize operations in support of Michigan State Athletics. Serve as the primary sport administrator for the Football program, providing leadership, guidance, and accountability to support competitive excellence and operational effectiveness. Oversee and provide strategic leadership for the following areas: Non-Philanthropic External Revenue Generation Capital Projects and Infrastructure Facilities Management Events and Operations Other units as assigned Lead departmental operational planning and execution to ensure efficient, effective, and fiscally responsible management of resources. In collaboration with Director of Athletics, provide leadership and support to the Spartan Athletic Foundation and the Athletics Business and Finance Office. Collaborate with coaches, administrators, university leaders, and external stakeholders to support championship-level performance across all sport programs. Serve as a member of the executive leadership team and participate in strategic decision-making related to athletics administration and Spartan Ventures operations. Perform other duties and special projects as assigned by the Director of Athletics. Serve as a key advisor to the Director of Athletics. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Masters Minimum Requirements Master's degree MBA, JD, Master's in Sport Administration, Business or related field 10-15 years of progressively responsible experience in athletics administration and senior leadership positions Demonstrated success leading complex organizations Required Application Materials Resume Cover Letter Review of Applications Begins On 09/29/2026 Website www.msuspartans.com MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 033d4269 Last Name (required) bd4bb51c Email (required) b26a227d Job Alert 11e153a4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Intercollegiate Athletics 10070478 Intercollegiate Athletics 10070478 Categories Ar