    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-tenure-system-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-101ba973-0e7e-498c-b3d6-8e6f7fa6a40d": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Tenure System",
      "description": "Assistant Professor-Tenure System - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Assistant Professor-Tenure System - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor-Tenure System Statistics & Probability 10032798 Faculty/Academic Staff Assistant Professor-Tenure System East Lansing, Michigan, United States Statistics & Probability 10032798 Area of Interest: Education/Training Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Sep 16 2026 Closing at: Sep 16 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Natural Science 1166557 Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary We seek outstanding candidates from all areas of statistics and applied probability . Candidates who develop innovative statistical or probabilistic theory and methodology, as well as those whose work is motivated by or contributes to important applications, are encouraged to apply. We are particularly interested in scholars whose research has the potential to address pressing issues in science and society through advances in statistical and probabilistic thinking, methodology, computation, and interdisciplinary collaboration. The successful candidates will be expected to develop and sustain internationally recognized research programs, pursue opportunities for external research funding, provide high-quality instruction and mentorship at the undergraduate and graduate levels, and contribute to the missions of the Department, College, and University. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Statistics or a closely related field Minimum Requirements Applicants must have a Ph.D. in statistics or a closely related field by the position start date. Candidates should demonstrate strong potential to develop an independent and impactful research program and a commitment to excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching and student mentoring. Desired Qualifications Applicants from all areas of statistics and applied probability will be considered. We particularly encourage applicants whose research demonstrates excellence and the potential for significant scholarly impact. Required Application Materials Applicants should submit the following materials electronically through the Michigan State University employment website: 1. A cover letter describing the applicant's interest in the position; 2. A curriculum vitae; 3. A research statement describing past accomplishments, current research, and future research directions; 4. A teaching and mentoring statement describing the applicant's experience and philosophy regarding undergraduate and graduate education and student mentorship; and 5. Three or more letters of reference that comment on the applicant’s research and teaching. Special Instructions Review of applications will begin on November 30, 2026 , and will continue until the positions are filled. Applications received by November 30, 2026, will receive full consideration. Questions regarding the positions may be directed to the search committee at STT.Search@msu.edu . Please note this is a union position represented by the Union for Tenure System Faculty. The university is working with the union to establish a collective bargaining agreement MSU is committed to providing a work environment that supports employees' work and personal life and offers employment assistance to the spouse or partner of candidates for faculty and academic staff positions. Review of Applications Begins On 11/30/2026 Website www.stt.natsci.msu.edu Department Statement The Department is distinctive in having strong research programs in both statistics and probability and offers a stimulating intellectual environment for interactions across these areas. The Department significantly added expertise in machine learning and artificial intelligence in recent years. The Department offers undergraduate, master's, and doctoral programs and contributes broadly to statistical and data science education across Michigan State University. Faculty members have opportunities to collaborate with researchers throughout MSU, a leading research university with strengths spanning the natural sciences, engineering, computational sciences, agriculture, environmental sciences, health and biomedical sciences, and the social sciences. Additional information about the Department of Statistics and Probability is available through the Department's website www.stt.natsci.msu.edu. MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 25a93eab Last Name (required) 9e21b359 Email (required) 6a73cd98 Job Alert 4998740c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Statistics & Probability 10032798 Statistics & Probability 10032798 Categories Area of Interest: Education/Training Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Education/Training Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Natural Science College Of Natural Science By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) bd6c3f6e Last Name (required) 053e18bb Email (required) c1f8708e Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Michigan State University is committed to safeguarding the privacy of personal data. To understand what type of information MSU Sites collects and how that information is used, view the MSU Privacy Statement . Visitors have the option of disabling or not accepting cookies by changing the preferences on their browser. If visitors disable cookies, they will still be able to use most sections of MSU Sites, but some sections may require the use of cookies. MSU also will not be able to tailor content to a visitor’s interests without cookies and a person will not be able to use any parts of MSU Sites that require a login. You consent to our cookies continue to browse this site. If you click on \"Accept essential only\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deterio