    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-scholar-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-a8d7034e-efad-458f-91d2-e198a000d386": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term Mechanical Engineering 10016576 Faculty/Academic Staff Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Mechanical Engineering 10016576 Area of Interest: Engineers/Architects Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Aug 7 2026 Closing at: Dec 1 2026 - 23:55 EST Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Engineering 1151902 Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary ​We cordially invite applications for a full-time postdoctoral scholar position at Michigan State University. The position will focus on the modeling, system design, and optimal power control of second-life batteries. The successful candidate will work with Dr. Huazhen Fang and other collaborators. The research aims to advance the technologies needed to repurpose retired electric-vehicle batteries for second-life applications. Such batteries often exhibit substantial variability in their usage and aging histories, internal conditions, remaining capacities, and power capabilities. To address these challenges, the successful candidate will pursue one or both of the following research directions: degradation-aware electrochemical modeling and second-life battery system design and optimal power control. The anticipated start date is October 2026, with the exact date negotiable. The initial appointment will be for one year, with the possibility of extension contingent upon research performance and the availability of funding. Salary will be commensurate with the candidate’s qualifications and experience while complying with Michigan State University policies. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Mechanical Engineering or closely related Minimum Requirements A recent Ph.D. degree in Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Power Electronics and Power Systems, Automation, Chemical Engineering, or a closely related field by the date of appointment. Doctoral research experience in one or more relevant areas, including battery modeling and control, power electronics, optimization, electrochemical energy storage, or related fields. Excellent record of scholarly accomplishments including publications and technical presentations on related subjects. Strong analytical skills, and the ability to formulate research questions, work independently, evaluate results critically, and document research methods clearly. Demonstrated communication (verbal and written) and leadership skills. Candidates will be evaluated on their research experience and communication skills, as evidenced by: (i) CV and cover letter, (ii) statement, (iii) prior research publications and/or patent applications, (iv) professional references, and (v) interview by videoconference. Desired Qualifications Record of research proposal development. History of advising and mentoring students for research. Required Application Materials The applicants should send the following documents: CV and cover letter describing educational background, research experience, publications, technical skills, and other research achievements, up to 2-page research statement, three representative research publications and/or patent applications, names and contact information of three referees. MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 284ad867 Last Name (required) 7f864f46 Email (required) 634bfc2b Job Alert 90e325cc Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Mechanical Engineering 10016576 Mechanical Engineering 10016576 Categories Area of Interest: Engineers/Architects Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Engineers/Architects Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Engineering College Of Engineering By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) b29654d6 Last Name (required) a1ca25e0 Email (required) 616a81ea Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell