    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/assistant-coach-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-cce9e822-fa82-483e-9cc5-3ad7d299e404": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Assistant Coach-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Assistant Coach-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Coach-Fixed Term Intercollegiate Athletics 10070478 Faculty/Academic Staff Assistant Coach-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Intercollegiate Athletics 10070478 Area of Interest: Athletics/Recreation Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Aug 27 2026 Closing at: Aug 27 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience Intercollegiate Athletics 1162834 Add to favorites View favorites Working/Functional Title Assistant Director, Athletic Performance Coach Position Summary The Assistant Director, Athletic Performance Coach is responsible for the oversight of Athletic Performance programming. Reporting to the Assistant AD / Director of Athletic Performance, the primary responsibilities of this role include the creation, implementation and evaluation of a comprehensive sport performance-training program. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities Assist the Assistant AD / Director of Athletic Performance/Olympic Sports in creating a championship strength and conditioning training environment and culture for men's and women's sports. Assist with implementing sport-specific programs based on peer-reviewed, evidence-based protocols to enhance the fitness, strength, power, and speed of intercollegiate athletes in the assigned sport(s). Implement a motivational environment where athletes strive for consistent elite-level performances. Assist with the implementation of individualized performance nutrition and body composition strategies developed in collaboration with Sports Medicine and Sports Nutrition staff to support athlete health, wellness, and performance goals. Collaborate effectively with coaches, sports medicine personnel, nutrition staff, and other stakeholders to support student-athlete development, health, wellness, and performance objectives. Supervise, mentor, and provide guidance to staff, graduate assistants, interns, and student employees supporting assigned programs and activities. Model and uphold organizational values, policies, procedures, and performance standards. Participate in departmental and cross-functional team meetings to support collaboration and operational effectiveness. Maintain accurate and confidential records related to student-athlete training programs, performance metrics, assessments, and participation, in accordance with applicable policies and regulations. Assist in maintaining a safe, organized, and professional training environment, including the proper care, maintenance, and inventory of equipment and facilities. Other duties as assigned. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Masters -Kinesiology, Exercise Science, or related field Minimum Requirements Master's degree in kinesiology or exercise science with at least three years of professional experience; or an equivalent combination of professional experience and education preferred. The following required certifications through one or both accredited strength and conditioning organizations must be maintained: the Strength & Conditioning Coach Certified (SCCC) by the Collegiate Strength & Conditioning Coaches Association (CSCCa), and/or the Certified Strength & Conditioning Specialist (CSCS) by the National Strength & Conditioning Association (NSCA). Required Application Materials Resume Cover Letter Summary of Physical Demands Ability to lift weights and demonstrate exercises. Website WWW.MSUSPARTANS.COM MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) b42088b7 Last Name (required) bda4071a Email (required) 8082e7d6 Job Alert 7699e273 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Intercollegiate Athletics 10070478 Intercollegiate Athletics 10070478 Categories Area of Interest: Athletics/Recreation Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Athletics/Recreation Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit Intercollegiate Athletics Intercollegiate Athletics By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the oppo