    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-tenure-system-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-2bf2e536-bb31-48a7-a9e5-4735dd2ce58e": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Tenure System",
      "description": "Assistant Professor-Tenure System - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Assistant Professor-Tenure System - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor-Tenure System Physics-Astronomy 10032666 Faculty/Academic Staff Assistant Professor-Tenure System East Lansing, Michigan, United States Physics-Astronomy 10032666 Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Sep 10 2026 Closing at: Sep 10 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Natural Science 1164944 Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary The Department of Physics & Astronomy at Michigan State University (MSU) invites applications for a tenure-system faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor holding an endowed Cowen Chair Professorship. Candidates should demonstrate the potential to lead an independent and world-class research program in the broad field of Condensed Matter Experiment. Topics of interest, listed in no specific order, include topological and quantum materials, quantum dynamics and coherent control, solid-state-based quantum information, non-equilibrium many-body physics, as well as optical and electronic properties of materials. Candidates must hold a Ph.D. in physics or a closely related area and are expected to build and maintain a sustainable research program that will complement and strengthen the existing experimental and theoretical efforts at MSU, make significant scholarly contributions, be effective as teachers and mentors, and engage in institutional and professional service. Please note that this is a union position represented by the Union of Tenure System Faculty (UTSF). The university is working with the union to establish a collective bargaining agreement. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Physics or a closely related area. Minimum Requirements Candidates must hold a Ph.D. in physics or a closely related area and are expected to build and maintain a sustainable research program in experimental condensed matter physics that will complement and strengthen the existing experimental and theoretical efforts at MSU, make significant scholarly contributions, be effective as teachers and mentors, and engage in institutional and professional service. Required Application Materials This position is listed on the MSU Applicant Page (https://jobs.msu.edu) , posting 1164944. Applications should be uploaded to MSU’s online job application site, https://jobs.msu.edu , and should include in a single pdf file: A cover letter that frames your application in the context of this position description. A CV, which should include a list of publications, contributed and invited talks, teaching and mentoring roles, leadership positions, contributions to the academic community, and efforts in public outreach. A statement highlighting past research successes and future research interests and plans for developing a sustainable research group. This statement should describe any collaborative and interdisciplinary research efforts and specify which lead-author publication the applicant would like the search committee to read. The research statement should not exceed four pages. A teaching statement describing the applicant’s plan for, and experience with, classroom teaching and mentoring in research. The teaching statement should not exceed two pages. Name, telephone, address, and email of three references to provide letters upon request. Special Instructions Please submit applications before the review of applications begins on November 30, 2026. Late submissions will be considered if qualified applicants have not yet been identified. Questions regarding this position may be directed to Prof. Norman Birge ( birge@msu.edu ). Review of Applications Begins On 11/30/2026 Website https://pa.msu.edu/ MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 7552ac88 Last Name (required) 0fe2e26c Email (required) 432fb2a3 Job Alert aa325695 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Physics-Astronomy 10032666 Physics-Astronomy 10032666 Categories Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Natural Science College Of Natural Science By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested