    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/research-associate-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-5d707528-fc7a-4832-ad0c-6f6bbaafb2af": {
      "title": "Research Associate-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Research Associate-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Research Associate-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Research Associate-Fixed Term Microbiology, Genetics, Immunology Cns 10032586 Faculty/Academic Staff Research Associate-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Microbiology, Genetics, Immunology Cns 10032586 Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Aug 27 2025 Closing at: Aug 27 2027 - 15:45 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Natural Science 1075879 Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary A Research Associate (Post-Doc) position is available in the laboratory of Dr. Zhiyong Xi in the Department of Microbiology, Genetics, & Immunology at Michigan State University. The position is available starting immediately with three years of funding guaranteed with a possibility of an extension based on progress and performance. The main project is to work on cutting-edge research to study the artificial symbiosis between the endosymbiotic bacterium Wolbachia and Anopheles malaria vectors. The project will center around establishing Wolbachia transinfection in Anopheles and dissecting genetic and environmental factors shaping Wolbachia-Anopheles symbiosis (See here: DOI: 10.1126/science.1236192 ; https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pntd.0012523 ). This includes exploring the interactions between various Wolbachia strains and Anopheles under diverse genetic backgrounds and environmental conditions. The applicant is expected to design and conduct experiments independently and clearly document results for use in presentations, manuscripts and grants. This is a full-time, 12-month fixed-term position with reappointment contingent on satisfactory performance and available funding Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate Minimum Requirements The applicant must have a PhD in the area of medical entomology, parasitology, microbiology/immunology/molecular biology or a related field and have a strong background in genetics. Strong quantitative and communication skills are required. Desired Qualifications Previous experience working in a BSL2 is desired but not required. Experience with developing Wolbachia for mosquito-borne disease control is preferred although not required. Required Application Materials Please submit a cover letter, CV, and the names and contact information for three references. Review of Applications Begins On 09/15/2025 Summary of Health Risks Some duties in this position may include the following health risks: -Exposure to human blood, serum, tissue and other body fluids; and materials covered under Universal Precautions. -Work with animals or unfixed animal tissue. Website https://mgi.natsci.msu.edu/ MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) b0ca7246 Last Name (required) 6c118294 Email (required) a6fee753 Job Alert 3df6aef2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Microbiology, Genetics, Immunology Cns 10032586 Microbiology, Genetics, Immunology Cns 10032586 Categories Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Natural Science College Of Natural Science By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) 5d1afba3 Last Name (required) d9b36e0c Email (required) f3023247 Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Michigan State University is committed to safeguarding the privacy of personal data. To understand what type of information MSU Sites collects and how that information is used, view the MSU Privacy Statement . Visitors have the option of disabling or not accepting cookies by changing the preferences on their browser. If visitors disable cookies, they will still be