    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/assistant-curator-east-lansing-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Curator",
      "description": "Assistant Curator - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Assistant Curator - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Curator Art Museum 10050506 Faculty/Academic Staff Assistant Curator East Lansing, Michigan, United States Art Museum 10050506 Area of Interest: Library/Museums/Archives Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Sep 8 2026 Closing at: Sep 8 2028 - 23:55 EDT 62000.00 University Arts And Collections 1164277 Add to favorites View favorites Working/Functional Title Assistant Curator Position Summary The Assistant Curator contributes to the museum’s overall curatorial vision and develops and produces timely, thoughtful, and relevant exhibitions, commissions, acquisitions, and programs. Following the museum’s strategic plan and curatorial vision, the Assistant Curator advances the museum’s broader goals of artistic excellence, public engagement, and experiential learning. The Assistant Curator supports exhibition development, acquisitions, and strategies to activate and interpret the collection, as well as developing new scholarship and publications. The position collaborates and partners with peers across other the museum to support this collective work. The Assistant Curator reports to the Senior Curator and Director of Curatorial Affairs. Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities: Exhibition Development: The Assistant Curator develops and implements both assigned and proposed museum exhibitions, developed in alignment with the museum’s strategic goals, ensuring the museum meets MSU’s standards of academic excellence in the planning, research, writing, and the development of exhibition programs and interpretation. The role ensures budget compliance and contracts meet MSU standards, in partnership with other museum team members. A meaningful element of the position is to assist in the development of major exhibitions under the purview of the Senior Curator and Director of Curatorial Affairs. Contribute to Collection Growth and Stewardship: The position contributes to the development and periodic review of the collection roadmap, supporting the museum’s collections strategy and ensuring it aligns with the museum’s long-term collections vision. This includes research on specific objects, proposing potential additions to the collection, ongoing contributions and updates to object files in accordance with best practices and field-wide standards. Grant Development: Participate in the curatorial team’s grant writing in support of exhibitions, programs, commissions, acquisitions, and publications, including contribution of ideas, gathering documentation and supplemental materials, and writing and managing individual grants. Support Fundraising and Donor Relations: In partnership with the Senior Curator and Director of Curatorial Affairs, the Museum Director, and university advancement team, the position helps to build relationships with artists, collectors, foundations, and donors. Cultivate Campus and Community Partnerships: The position regularly represents the museum and the curatorial vision of the institution with partners on and off campus. This includes deepening the museum’s ties to MSU students, faculty, and staff, and nurturing relationships with local and regional institutions and communities. The Assistant Curator supports these efforts through relationship-building, educational engagements, and developing curatorial proposals with partners. Serve as Museum Ambassador Locally and Nationally: The position serves as an institutional ambassador, representing the museum to professional networks, peer institutions, academic collaborators, and the public. This position advances the museum’s national and international profile through participation in professional conferences, scholarly publications, and other curatorial and academic opportunities. Committee Coordination: As assigned and working closely with the Senior Curator and Director of Curatorial Affairs, Assistant Curators coordinate the activities of the Collections Committee. This includes the scheduling of committee meetings, compilation of documents, setting agendas, taking minutes, maintaining committee membership records, and contributing to the priorities and vision for each. The Assistant Curator plays a vital role in exhibition development, as both lead curator or in support of other projects. For most exhibition projects, an advisory committee is formed to support the work of the museum, and the coordination of this advisory committee is likewise either led or supported by the Assistant Curator. Teaching: This position may play a teaching role in museum and other campus programs (e.g., participating in classes, presentations, and lectures, or providing experiential learning opportunities to undergraduate/graduate students who are working on museum projects. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Masters -Desired area of study in Art History, Curatorial Practice, Arts Administration or related field Desired Degree Masters Minimum Requirements Experience assisting with the development of thematic and monographic art exhibitions and publications; Experience assisting interdisciplinary projects and supporting strategic partnerships with diverse stakeholders; and three or more years of curatorial/museum experience. Broad knowledge of art history and developments in curatorial practice and theory, along with a focused engagement with key issues in the field. Three years of experience working within the museum field, or related cultural organizations. Desired Qualifications Three to five years of experience working within the museum field, or related cultural organizations. An established history of publications, conference presentations, lecturing, and educational experience especially at the university or college level. Required Application Materials Cover letter describing your interest in the position and how it fits with your career goals, educational background and work experience that prepares you for the responsibilities of this role. Curriculum vitae or resume Contact information for three professional referees who can speak to the applicants skills for this position Review of Applications Begins On 09/29/2026 Website https://broadmuseum.msu.edu/ MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) a8b44a8b Last Name (required) 1d135820 Email (required) 53dcf803 Job Alert 00c0f620 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Art Museum 10050506 Art Museum 10050506 Categories Area of Interest: Library/Museums/Archives Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Library/Museums/Archives Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit University Arts And Collections University Arts And Collections By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Biddin