    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/associate-dean-management-east-lansing-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Dean-Management",
      "description": "Associate Dean-Management - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Associate Dean-Management - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Associate Dean-Management Veterinary Medicine Dean 10046908 Faculty/Academic Staff Associate Dean-Management East Lansing, Michigan, United States Veterinary Medicine Dean 10046908 Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Veterinary/Animal Care Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Academic Management Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Sep 8 2026 Closing at: Sep 8 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Veterinary Medicine 1164600 Add to favorites View favorites Working/Functional Title Associate Dean for Professional Education Position Summary The Michigan State University College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications and nominations for the position of Associate Dean for Professional Education. The successful candidate takes on this role at the College at an exciting time as we launch our Veterinary College of the Future Initiative - a bold effort to re-imagine veterinary education through educational innovation, inter-professional learning, emerging technologies, and evidence-based teaching practices. This is a unique opportunity for an accomplished educational leader to shape the future of veterinary education while preparing graduates to thrive in an increasingly complex and collaborative profession. This is a 50% appointment for a faculty member with a demonstrated scholarly interest in curriculum development, educational innovation, outcomes assessment, and continuous quality improvement. The position reports directly to the Dean and works closely with department chairs, associate deans, executive directors and other college leadership, faculty, staff, and students. This is a five-year, renewable-term appointment, contingent upon performance. An annual administrative stipend will be provided. The Associate Dean for Professional Education (ADPE) provides strategic and operational leadership for the Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM) curriculum and serves as a key member of the College's academic leadership team. Working in partnership with the Associate Dean for Student Engagement and Success, the ADPE will monitor student success and use educational outcomes and learner feedback to continually refine the DVM curriculum, ensuring students are supported throughout their educational journey and prepared to enter the veterinary profession. The ADPE will also collaborate closely with the Office of Health and Well-being to foster an educational environment that promotes student well-being, resilience, inclusivity, and professional development. Beyond the DVM curriculum, the Associate Dean will work collaboratively with the Associate Deans for Veterinary Nursing and Graduate Studies to advance innovative educational opportunities across the College. As one of only four colleges of veterinary medicine in North America with an embedded veterinary nursing program, and with continued strategic investment in our DVM/PhD program, Michigan State University offers exceptional opportunities to develop inter-professional, team-based educational models and innovative pathways for training future clinician-scientists. The Associate Dean will oversee the Office of Professional Education, including DVM programmatic teams (pre-clinical education, clinical education, and outcomes assessment), while partnering with faculty and academic leaders to implement leading-edge educational approaches that advance the goals of the Veterinary College of the Future Initiative. Key Responsibilities The Associate Dean will: Provide strategic and operational leadership for the DVM curriculum. Partner with the Associate Dean for Student Engagement and Success to monitor student success and continually improve the DVM program through data-informed innovation and student support. Collaborate with the Office of Health and Well-being to promote student well-being, resilience, inclusivity, and professional identity formation. Work collaboratively with the Associate Deans for Veterinary Nursing and Graduate Studies to develop innovative educational opportunities that strengthen inter-professional education and clinician-scientist training. Advance the Veterinary College of the Future Initiative by fostering innovative educational approaches, emerging technologies, and evidence-based teaching practices. Lead curriculum development, outcomes assessment, continuous quality improvement, and educational data analytics for the DVM program. Foster faculty development and scholarship in teaching, assessment, and curriculum design. Provide leadership for the infrastructure supporting pre-clinical education, clinical education, clinical skills, and outcomes assessment. Represent the College on relevant University and external committees. Support AVMA Council on Education accreditation and institutional reporting. Why Michigan State? Michigan State University is committed to preparing the next generation of veterinary professionals through innovation, collaboration, and a One Health perspective. Few institutions offer the breadth of educational opportunities found at MSU, including: One of only four colleges of veterinary medicine in North America with an embedded veterinary nursing program, creating exceptional opportunities for inter-professional education and team-based healthcare. Continued strategic investment in DVM/PhD education, supporting the development of future clinician-scientists. A comprehensive Office of Health and Well-being that integrates embedded counselors, veterinary social work, well-being programming, and initiatives that foster an inclusive learning environment. A collaborative academic leadership model that brings together expertise from across the college to continuously strengthen our academic programs. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -A DVM, MD (or equivalent), and/or PhD Desired Degree Other -Training in professional education Minimum Requirements A DVM, MD (or equivalent), and/or PhD Demonstrated commitment to professional education Exceptional leadership and management abilities. Commitment to excellence in teaching and educational leadership Experience in curriculum development, program evaluation, accreditation, and assessment Desired Qualifications Experience leading curricular innovation across complex academic environments Training or qualifications in professional education Required Application Materials A current curriculum vitae. A letter describing the applicant's interest in the position, relevant leadership experience, and vision for professional education. A statement describing the applicant's contributions to advancing the mission and values of the Michigan State University College of Veterinary Medicine. Special Instructions Interested candidates are encouraged to contact the search committee chair, James Wagner at wagnerja@msu.edu with any questions or requests for additional information. Applications (curriculum vitae and a letter of interest) will be reviewed beginning September 15, 2026. Review of Applications Begins On 09/15/2026 Website cvm.msu.edu Department Statement The mission of the Michigan State University College of Veterinary Medicine is: Learn. Discover. Heal. Protect. MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 8f671927 Last Name (required) bd3b0ccf Email (required) 0948d709 Job Alert 84d54a52 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Veterinary Medicine Dean 10046908 Veterinary Medicine Dean 10046908 Categories Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Veterinary/Animal Care Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Academic Management Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Veterinary/Animal Care Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Academic Management Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Veterinary Medicine College Of Veterinary Medicine By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) d2666e91 Last Name (required) 996b972a Email (required) acab26c1 Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Michigan State University is committed to safeguarding the privacy of personal data. To understand what type of information MSU Sites collects and how that information is used, view the MSU Privacy Statement . Visitors have the option of disabling or not accepting cookies by changing the preferences on their browser. If visitors disable cookies, they will still be able to use most sections of MSU Sites, but some sections may require the use of cookies. MSU also will not be able to tailor content to a visitor’s interests without cookies and a person will not be able to use any parts of MSU Sites that require a login. You consent to our cookies continue to browse this site. If you click on \"Accept essential only\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the My Profile link on the top right of the browser window. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a unit"
