    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-scholar-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-6d21bcf2-eeb5-4d91-91b2-ee1bddd29c0b": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term Horticulture Anr 10002410 Faculty/Academic Staff Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Horticulture Anr 10002410 Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Sep 8 2026 Closing at: Sep 8 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Agriculture And Nat Resources 1163430 Add to favorites View favorites Working/Functional Title Postdoctoral Scholar Fixed-Term in the Barry Lab. Position Summary A postdoctoral researcher position is available in the Department of Horticulture at Michigan State University to work with Dr. Cornelius Barry ( https://www.canr.msu.edu/people/dr_cornelius_barry ) and Dr. Kevin Walker ( https://www.chemistry.msu.edu/faculty-research/faculty-members/walker-kevin.aspx ) on a collaborative project to elucidate alkaloid biosynthesis pathways in the Solanaceae (potato) family. The initial appointment is for one year, renewable for up to a total of four years dependent on performance and availability of funding. We are seeking a highly motivated scientist with demonstrated expertise in plant biochemistry and metabolomics. Applicants should have a strong interest in plant specialized metabolism, excellent problem solving and analytical skills, be detail oriented, and possess strong organizational capabilities. The successful candidate must be able to work independently and as part of a team to design and lead experiments, perform data analysis, present data to scientific audiences, contribute to reports, and co-write manuscripts. Some mentoring and supervision of undergraduate researchers may be required. MSU is a Land Grant Institution located in East Lansing, Michigan with a vibrant and highly collaborative plant sciences community and over 150 faculty engaged in basic and applied research. Researchers have access to state-of-the-art facilities and numerous opportunities exist for postdoctoral scholars to enhance their training and professional development. As an institution of higher learning, Michigan State University is committed to providing a safe environment for its students, faculty, and staff in support of its educational mission. With this commitment, the University conducts criminal background checks and professional misconduct reviews of all applicants for employment in faculty, academic staff, and executive management searches. Professional Misconduct Review A professional misconduct review is a prerequisite for a candidate to be selected for this position. Applicants will be asked to disclose whether they are subject to any pending investigation, findings or sanctions related to professional misconduct. Professional misconduct includes misconduct related to a person’s employment, including, but not limited to, theft, embezzlement, research integrity, discrimination, or harassment under civil rights laws and policies, including protected identity harassment, sexual harassment, sexual misconduct (sexual assault, sexual exploitation, dating violence, domestic violence, stalking, etc.), and retaliation. All applicants will be asked to sign an authorization and release, which authorizes the University to contact the candidate’s current and former employers, for a period of 7 years prior to the date of application, related to any pending investigations, findings of responsibility and/or sanctions related to professional misconduct. Nothing will be sent to current or former employers unless the candidate reaches the semi-finalist stage. The existence of professional misconduct history does not automatically exclude a candidate from employment. The University will assess the history, including any information provided by the candidate, in determining whether it is compatible with the position. The University may decline to hire a candidate based on the professional misconduct review. All records obtained from external employers will be kept in a secure location, separate from personnel files. If an applicant fails to sign the authorization and release, the application will be deemed incomplete and will be withdrawn. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Biochemistry or a plant science-related discipline. Minimum Requirements Demonstrated experience in plant biochemistry and mass spectrometry-based metabolomics. Desired Qualifications Experience in molecular biology and enzymology. Experience in plant genetic manipulation through gene-silencing, CRISPR, or mutant analysis. Experience in plant natural product research. A strong record of effective oral and written communication, including publishing in peer-reviewed journals and presenting scientific results at conferences and meetings. Excellent interpersonal skills. Required Application Materials Please provide a 1-2 page cover letter that describes your research experiences and interests, a current CV, and names and contact information for three references. Special Instructions Anticipated start date is October 1, 2026. Review of Applications Begins On 09/15/2026 Website hrt.msu.edu MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) ba970fe9 Last Name (required) 4a520b77 Email (required) 29c09552 Job Alert 2760debc Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Horticulture Anr 10002410 Horticulture Anr 10002410 Categories Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Agriculture And Nat Resources College Of Agriculture And Nat Resources By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) 9d254b49 Last Name (required) b8c89588 Email (required) 81623967 Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages 