    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-tenure-system-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-23bc86d0-5d37-4db2-bfe7-e47a565d88ce": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Tenure System",
      "description": "Assistant Professor-Tenure System - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Assistant Professor-Tenure System - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor-Tenure System Economics 10038238 Faculty/Academic Staff Assistant Professor-Tenure System East Lansing, Michigan, United States Economics 10038238 Area of Interest: Education/Training Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Aug 24 2026 Closing at: Aug 24 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Social Science 1155444 Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary Michigan State University actively promotes a dynamic research and learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. The Department of Economics at Michigan State University in East Lansing invites applications for a tenure-system Assistant Professor in microeconomic theory with an anticipated start date of August 16, 2027. We are especially interested in candidates doing work in information economics but are open to excellent candidates in all subfields of microeconomic theory. Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026, and will continue until a suitable candidate is identified. Please note that this is a union position represented by the Union of Tenure System Faculty (UTSF). The university is working with the union to establish a collective bargaining agreement Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Economics or related field Minimum Requirements Research interest primarily in information economics or related subfields of microeconomic theory. A well-defined research agenda with a track record of scholarly contributions and potential for high-impact peer review publication. Doctorate (A PhD is expected to be conferred by August 1, 2027.) Desired Qualifications Potential for high-quality instruction and mentoring at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Potential for pursuing external funding Demonstrated ability and/or potential to provide service to the Department, the University, and the profession, and to work with students and faculty from a variety of backgrounds. Required Application Materials All applicants must apply online at https://careers.msu.edu . All applications should be accompanied by a curriculum vitae (CV), cover letter, a list of your publications with hyperlinks to articles and/or up to two unpublished working papers in PDF format, statement on teaching, and a list of references who can provide letters of recommendation (names and emails only). If relevant, please include a list of grants received (including funding amounts) and sponsored research in your vitae. Special Instructions Questions should be directed to heardkir@msu.edu. Review of Applications Begins On 11/01/2026 Website http://econ.msu.edu Department Statement The mission of the Department of Economics at Michigan State University consists of three interrelated components: providing the highest quality instruction to our undergraduate and graduate students, conducting leading-edge research in economics, and providing leadership and service to our professional communities. As a unit in a major land-grant university, we are committed to excelling in all three components of our mission. To learn more about the department, our faculty, and our PhD and undergraduate programs, please visit our website at http://econ.msu.edu . MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 1920f9a6 Last Name (required) 71d64a47 Email (required) e64edd50 Job Alert 02fb877a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Economics 10038238 Economics 10038238 Categories Area of Interest: Education/Training Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Area of Interest: Education/Training Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Social Science College Of Social Science By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) e624dd9b Last Name (required) dc6d8a9d Email (required) 201856da Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment