    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-scholar-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-75ad424a-abed-4e8d-b789-22036e7fce98": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term Biochemistry & Molecular Biology Cns 10032098 Faculty/Academic Staff Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Biochemistry & Molecular Biology Cns 10032098 Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Aug 28 2026 Closing at: Aug 28 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Natural Science 1156447 Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary The Lundquist Laboratory Group is seeking a Researcher & Laboratory Manager to play a pivotal role in advancing our research on plastoglobule lipid droplets and their involvement in photosynthetic and phospho-regulation. In this dual-capacity role, you will dedicate approximately 20% of your time to operational leadership, ensuring seamless daily lab function through budget management, chemical/supply inventory control, safety protocol adherence, and digital outreach. The other 80% of your time will be dedicated to active scientific investigation, where you will integrate wet-lab techniques ( e.g. , immunoblotting, protein phosphorylation assays, cellular ultrastructure investigation, lipidomics, proteomics, etc.) with computational approaches ( e.g. , protein-protein interaction and structural modeling) to drive impactful discoveries. Detailed description of work/duties: Laboratory Management & Operations (20%) Operational Oversight: Manage daily laboratory operations, resource purchasing, and maintenance of chemical and supply inventories. Safety & Compliance: Ensure full compliance with institutional environmental health and safety (EHS) protocols and guidelines. Digital Presence: Maintain and update the laboratory website to reflect current research, publications, and team updates. Scientific Research & Execution (80%) Experimental Design & Execution: Plan and perform advanced biochemical, molecular, cellular, and computational experiments to investigate plastoglobule function. Wet-Lab Techniques: Conduct specialized assays, including protein phosphorylation studies, immunoblotting, lipidomics, proteomics, protein-protein interaction studies and/or cellular ultrastructural investigations. Mentoring and supervision: Train and supervise undergraduate and graduate trainees in experimental design, wet-lab protocols, and data analysis to ensure research quality and laboratory safety. Communication: Assist in preparation of scientific manuscripts and research talks. Computational Modeling: Utilize bioinformatic and computational tools for structural modeling and protein-protein interaction analyses. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -biochemistry, molecular biology, cell biology or related field Minimum Requirements PhD in biochemistry, molecular biology, cell biology or related field. Demonstrable experience with design, execution and communication of bench (wet-lab) research. Excellent organizational and management skills. Excellent multi-tasking and time-management skills. Desired Qualifications Demonstrated experience with plant biochemical or molecular biological research such as gene cloning, in vitro kinase assays, lipid profiling, protein-protein interaction assays. Familiarity with gene cloning, heterologous protein expression, in vitro kinase assays, immunoblotting, photosynthetic measurements and/or confocal and electron microscopy. Required Application Materials Cover letter outlining qualifications and reason for interest Current CV/resume Contact information for at least three references Review of Applications Begins On 08/31/2026 Summary of Health Risks formaldehyde Website https://www.lundquist-lab.net/ MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) b9a08236 Last Name (required) d678168c Email (required) e6813878 Job Alert 1a9d8fb3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Biochemistry & Molecular Biology Cns 10032098 Biochemistry & Molecular Biology Cns 10032098 Categories Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Natural Science College Of Natural Science By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait..