      "description": "Ast Prof-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Ast Prof-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Ast Prof-Fixed Term History 10038404 Faculty/Academic Staff Ast Prof-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States History 10038404 Area of Interest: Education/Training Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Aug 24 2026 Closing at: Aug 23 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Social Science 1141484 Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary Michigan State University actively promotes a dynamic research and learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. The Department of History at Michigan State University invites applications for a pool of qualified fixed-term Assistant Professors to teach one or more undergraduate or graduate-level courses per semester. These positions could be part-time or full time, and vary by semester, depending on the needs of the Department. It is possible that no positions are needed in some semesters. Applicants in this pool are reviewed when the Department has immediate needs and positions would begin as early as January 1, 2027. Courses would be offered during the regular academic year (AY) when available. Candidates must be qualified to teach in at least ONE of the following fields: United States History Latin American History Asian History European History African History Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Doctorate – History in US, Latin America, Asia, Europe or Africa Minimum Requirements A Ph.D. or equivalent degree required by date of hire. Candidates must have a demonstrated record of teaching excellence and/or significant work experience in one of the following fields: U.S. History, Latin American History, African History, Asian History, or European History. Desired Qualifications Experience teaching undergraduate courses of varying enrollment sizes. Experience supervising or working with teaching assistants. Required Application Materials Cover Letter that includes the areas of teaching interest. Resume/CV. Name and contact information for three professional references. Special Instructions Review of applications will begin when courses become available and will continue until positions are filled. Questions regarding this position can be addressed to the Search Committee Chair and the Department Chairperson, Dr. Michael Stamm at stamm@msu.edu . Review of Applications Begins On 09/21/2026 Website HISTORY.MSU.EDU MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 2899b7c1 Last Name (required) c4313f2e Email (required) 0f22672b Job Alert 1cfd7345 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments History 10038404 History 10038404 Categories Area of Interest: Education/Training Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union A