    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/specialist-advisor-continuing-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-333f097f-6322-4aa6-92b1-a84505ea5e00": {
      "title": "Specialist - Advisor-Continuing",
      "description": "Specialist - Advisor-Continuing - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Specialist - Advisor-Continuing - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Specialist - Advisor-Continuing Nursing 10033616 Faculty/Academic Staff Specialist - Advisor-Continuing East Lansing, Michigan, United States Nursing 10033616 Area of Interest: Advising/Counseling Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Continuing System Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Aug 24 2026 Closing at: Aug 24 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Nursing 1155136 Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary The College of Nursing is seeking applications for a Specialist-Advisor in our Office of Student Affairs. The Academic Advisor will assist in the planning, coordination, and implementation of initiatives that advance the College of Nursing’s mission, vision, and strategic goals related to advancing excellence in undergraduate recruitment, admissions, enrollment, and academic advising. This position is responsible for supporting or co-leading processes that enhance student success and contribute to the College’s strategic objectives through effective academic advising, program coordination, assessment, and data-informed decision-making. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong record of working in an academic environment and a commitment to access, opportunity, and excellence. Experience in academic advising, student recruitment, program or project management, and administrative operations is essential. Responsibilities include but are not limited to: Academic Advising Provide proactive, student-centered academic advising to prospective and current undergraduate students regarding university, college, and program requirements. Monitor and track students’ academic progress toward degree completion, identifying and addressing opportunity barriers to success. Conduct graduation checks to ensure timely progress and degree certification. Event Planning, Service & Committee Work Coordinate, plan, and participate in events hosted by the College of Nursing’s Office of Student Affairs including but not limited to new student, graduation, and recruitment events. Serve on university-wide and college-level committees to represent the Office of Student Affairs and support institutional initiatives. Teaching Teach at least one section annually of the UGS 110 seminar for Pre-nursing students. Standard working hours are Monday through Friday from 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Occasional evenings and weekend events/responsibilities will be required. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Masters -in Student Affairs, Higher Education or related field Minimum Requirements Master’s degree in Student Affairs, Higher Education Administration, or a related field. Minimum of one year of experience in academic advising and/or student recruitment within a higher education setting. Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, including experience in public speaking. Strong organizational and time management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment while maintaining accuracy and attention to detail. Demonstrated ability to deliver high-quality customer service and exercise sound judgment with minimal supervision. Proven ability to collect, analyze, and interpret data to support student success and inform advising practices. Demonstrated innovative problem-solving skills and the ability to implement creative, practical solutions to complex challenges. Evidence of the ability to work collaboratively and constructively across multiple levels of a complex organization, building consensus and fostering positive working relationships with diverse populations. Ability to lift to 30 pounds. Possession of a valid driver’s license. Desired Qualifications Evidence of ongoing commitment to professional development in higher education, advising, or student success. Teaching and/or presentation experience with college students. Experience using complex student information systems and databases. Familiarity with the specific academic requirements and curricular structure of Nursing or Health Professions programs. Required Application Materials Resume Cover letter A list including three professional references with contact information Review of Applications Begins On 09/10/2026 Summary of Physical Demands lifting 50 pounds or more with frequent lifting and/or carrying of objects weighing 25 pounds or more Website WWW.NURSING.MSU.EDU Department Statement The Michigan State University College of Nursing has been training the next generations of nurses since its founding as the Department of Nursing Education in 1950. We believe in the power of research, practice and education to affect lasting change and to improve health outcomes in our communities. We do this through recruiting top faculty, staff and students and continuously staying at the forefront of changes in the profession. MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) e80a68f4 Last Name (required) 8f3e408b Email (required) e3deb3f6 Job Alert f7bfd771 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns