    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-scholar-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-1647ebc8-e2e6-4b7e-9bd4-e83080a565a4": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term Chemistry 10032142 Faculty/Academic Staff Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Chemistry 10032142 Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Aug 20 2026 Closing at: Aug 20 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Natural Science 1153921 Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary The Kim Lab at MSU Chemistry is seeking a Postdoctoral Scholar to conduct research on the growth and characterization of magnetic hybrid layered semiconductors using a metal-organic chemical vapor deposition (MOCVD) system. The successful candidate will contribute to a project aimed at achieving high magnetic dopant concentrations and dopant activity, and studying the resulting magnetic, structural, and photonic properties. Responsibilities include: Operating and maintaining a home-built MOCVD system Growing and characterizing doped and undoped single-crystals via optical microscopy, spectroscopy, electron microscopy, and X-ray techniques Conducting temperature- and field-dependent magnetic (EPR, SQUID) and optical (steady-state and time-resolved PL, magneto-PL) measurements to probe magnetic ordering and spin-polarized light emission Mentoring graduate and undergraduate researchers, and contributing to manuscript and grant preparation Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate Minimum Requirements PhD in Chemistry Physics Materials Science or related field any research experience Desired Qualifications Research experience with low-dimensional or dilute magnetic semiconductors, 2D magnetic materials, or related quantum/spintronic materials Experience with vapor-phase synthesis techniques (CVD/MOCVD, MBE, ALD, or similar) of semiconductors or hybrid/perovskite materials Hands-on experience with structural and magnetic characterization techniques such as XRD, SQUID magnetometry, and EPR Experience with optical/photoluminescence spectroscopy, including temperature-dependent, time-resolved, or polarization-resolved PL measurements Familiarity with electron microscopy (TEM/STEM) Strong record of peer-reviewed publications and evidence of independent research initiative Good communication skills and experience mentoring junior researchers Required Application Materials Cover letter, curriculum vitae, names and email addresses of 2-3 references Review of applications will begin on September 3, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Website https://www.chemistry.msu.edu/ MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 0b42d9ce Last Name (required) 4595b0c0 Email (required) 98b13059 Job Alert 8aa580f9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Chemistry 10032142 Chemistry 10032142 Categories Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Natural Science College Of Natural Science By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) a7db5d0a Last Name (required) 2a4d336b Email (required) 16f43e9a Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Michigan State University is committed to safeguarding the privacy of personal data. To understand what type of information MSU Sites collects and how that information is used, view the MSU Privacy Statement . Visitors have the option of disabling or not accepting cookies by changing the preferences on their browser. If visitors disable cookies, they will still be able to use most sections of MSU Sites, but some sections may require the use of cookies. MSU also will not be able to tailor content to a visitor’s i