    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-scholar-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-a4c9d337-579c-419f-b782-e5bb02751a41": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term Microbiology, Genetics, Immunology Chm 10022586 Faculty/Academic Staff Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Microbiology, Genetics, Immunology Chm 10022586 Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Jul 20 2026 Closing at: Jun 20 2028 - 16:45 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Human Medicine 1148598 Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary Postdoctoral positions funded by the NIH and MSU Research Foundation are open in the laboratory of Dr. Dohun Pyeon ( http://www.pyeonlab.org/ ) at Michigan State University. Our research group is uniquely positioned to carry out basic and translational cancer research by integrating patient specimens, unique mouse models, in vitro cell culture systems, recombinant virus production, genome-wide CRISPR, small-molecule screens, and single-cell analyses. Successful candidates will lead projects to define the mechanisms of virus-driven cancer immune evasion and to develop novel cancer immunotherapy targeting newly discovered immune regulators. These positions are supported for first-year postdoctoral scholars who are committed to building an independent research program through NIH career development (K) awards, and applicants must therefore be within the first year of postdoctoral training at the time of appointment. Candidates must hold a recent Ph.D. and/or M.D. in a related field and have lead-author publications in top-tier journals, excellent communication and organizational skills, and the ability to work independently within a research team. Expertise in cancer immunology, drug development, and/or mouse models is highly desirable. We provide a competitive salary at the NIH postdoctoral stipend level, excellent benefits, and one-on-one mentoring toward K award submission and a successful independent research career. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Terminal -Cancer immunology or a closely related field. Minimum Requirements A recent Ph.D. and/or M.D. in a related field, no more than one year of prior postdoctoral training at the time of appointment, and at least one lead-author publication in a top-tier research journal. Desired Qualifications A demonstrated commitment to building an independent research program through NIH career development (K) awards, expertise in cancer immunology, drug development, and/or mouse models, excellent communication and organizational skills, and the ability to work independently within a research team. Required Application Materials Cover letter, CV, and the contact information of three referees. Review of Applications Begins On 08/01/2026 Summary of Health Risks Some duties may include the following exposure to health risks: Exposure to human blood, serum, tissue and other body fluids; and materials covered under Universal Precautions. Work with animals or unfixed animal tissue. Website https://mgi.natsci.msu.edu/ MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign U