    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-full-professor-tenure-system-east-lansing-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Tenure System",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Tenure System - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Tenure System - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Tenure System Finance 10008339 Faculty/Academic Staff Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Tenure System East Lansing, Michigan, United States Finance 10008339 Area of Interest: Financial/Accounting Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Aug 13 2026 Closing at: Aug 13 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience Eli Broad College Of Business 1152169 Add to favorites View favorites Working/Functional Title Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Tenure System Position Summary The Department of Finance in the Eli Broad College of Business seeks applications for an Assistant/Associate/Full Professor appointment. Successful applicants will teach Corporate Finance, Investments, Risk Management, Behavioral Finance, Financial Data Analytics, and International Finance. Candidates for Assistant Professor should exhibit strong potential for high-quality research that is likely to result in top-level publications and national recognition. Associate/Full Professor candidates must have an established national reputation for original and influential research and demonstrable evidence that they will continue to grow their national status. Candidates are expected to complete all requirements for the Ph.D. in Finance or related field by June 30, 2027. The position will start on August 16, 2027. The department offers a collegial, research-driven environment with substantial resources to support ambitious scholarship and professional engagement. Please note this is a union position represented by the Union for Tenure System Faculty. The university is working with the union to establish a collective bargaining agreement. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Terminal -Finance, Economics, Financial Economics, or related field Minimum Requirements This position requires a Ph.D. degree from an accredited university. Candidates must have a demonstrated record of teaching excellence. Specific areas of expertise for this position include Corporate Finance, Investments, Risk Management, Behavioral Finance, Financial Data Analytics, and International Finance. Candidates must be able to teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Desired Qualifications Applicants must have a Ph.D. in Finance, financial economics, or related fields. Assistant Professor candidates should exhibit strong potential for high-quality research that is likely to result in top-level publications and national recognition. Successful seasoned candidates will demonstrate a sustained publication record in top-tier journals, a commitment to high-quality teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels, a record of service that advances the profession and academic community, and Associate/Full Professor candidates must have an established national reputation for original and influential research and demonstrable evidence that they will continue to grow their national status. Required Application Materials To be considered for this position, please submit a CV, names of three references, and evidence of teaching effectiveness (if available). Special Instructions Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. To ensure full consideration, please apply by November 20, 2026. Early applications, especially from experienced candidates, are strongly encouraged. Further questions may be directed to the following mailbox: financerecruiting@broad.msu.edu Review of Applications Begins On 11/20/2026 Website broad.msu.edu/finance MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) b8bb77bd Last Name (required) 07075363 Email (required) fa726674 Job Alert 4d87f68e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Finance 10008339 Finance 10008339 Categories Area of Interest: Financial/Accounting Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Area of Interest: Financial/Accounting Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Tenure System Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit Eli Broad College Of Business Eli Broad College Of Business By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Exp