    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-scholar-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-e4d90b39-b467-4a18-aee3-aad3d14f6cba": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term Create For Stem 40000120 Faculty/Academic Staff Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Create For Stem 40000120 Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Aug 10 2026 Closing at: Aug 10 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Natural Science 1150883 Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary The postdoctoral scholar will join a collaborative research team in the College of Natural Science and the CREATE for STEM Institute to support research on AI-assisted formative assessment and feedback in high school science classrooms. The position focuses on analyzing student responses to three-dimensional science learning tasks, including written explanations and student-generated models, and contributing to the development and refinement of generative AI–based feedback. The postdoctoral scholar will participate in classroom implementation studies examining how students and teachers use AI-generated feedback to support science learning. The initial appointment is for one year, with the possibility of renewal for a second year based on performance and funding. The postdoctoral scholar will work closely with the project PI, Dr. Kevin Haudek and collaborate with other project faculty to: 1) analyze student responses to assessment tasks using AI-supported tools and rubrics; 2) develop and refine formative feedback for student explanations and models; 3) help design, test, and refine GenAI feedback tools, including prompt development and review of AI-generated outputs;; 4) collect, organize, and analyze classroom data, including student engagement and performance; 5) conduct and analyze think-alouds and/or interviews with high school students and teachers about feedback and the use of the AI system; 6) support teacher-facing implementation activities and professional development as needed; 7) assist with project management and 8) contribute to project reports, publications, and conference presentations. The postdoctoral scholar will collaborate with faculty, other postdoctoral researchers and graduate students in Michigan State University's CREATE for STEM Institute ( http://www.create4stem.msu.edu/ ). Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -science education or a Ph.D. in a science discipline Minimum Requirements Candidates are expected to hold a Ph.D. in science education or a Ph.D. in a science discipline, preferably in biology, chemistry or closely related field with relevant educational research experience. Desired Qualifications Candidates with experience using AI to support student science learning, designing and analyzing assessments, conducting discipline‑based education research in chemistry or biology, and applying mixed‑methods research approaches. Required Application Materials Cover letter Resume/CV One page statement of research interests Names and emails of 3 references Review of Applications Begins On 08/21/2026 Website http://www.create4stem.msu.edu/ MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) ef00472d Last Name (required) d78c85a5 Email (required) fdf981e1 Job Alert ac866d4c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Create For Stem 40000120 Create For Stem 40000120 Categories Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Natural Science College Of Natural Science By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) c0299928 Last Name (required) 7f7b6259 Email (required) 9ff1e8b9 Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Cand