    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/inst-ast-prof-asc-prof-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-78396a0a-50ba-4d58-952b-393710b62571": {
      "title": "Inst/Ast Prof/Asc Prof - Fixed Term",
      "description": "Inst/Ast Prof/Asc Prof - Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Inst/Ast Prof/Asc Prof - Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Inst/Ast Prof/Asc Prof - Fixed Term Economics 10038238 Faculty/Academic Staff Inst/Ast Prof/Asc Prof - Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Economics 10038238 Area of Interest: Education/Training Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Jul 8 2025 Closing at: Jul 8 2027 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Social Science 1055320 Add to favorites View favorites Working/Functional Title Inst/Ast Prof/Asc Prof - Fixed Term Position Summary The Michigan State University Department of Economics seeks qualified candidates for the following Fixed Term position: Instructor, Assistant Professor or Associate Professor to teach students in economics and economics-related courses, with rank determined by degree and years of experience. Duties include: preparing the course; holding lectures; reviewing and grading assignments; advising students; submitting final grades; upholding departmental teaching standards; communicating with departmental leadership to ensure that the courses are completed appropriately. Appointment level will be made commensurate with degree and experience. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Economics or closely related field required. Minimum Requirements Required Degree Fixed Term Instructor: Masters’ in Economics or closely related field required. Fixed Term Assistant Professor: PhD in Economics or closely related field required. Fixed Term Associate Professor: PhD in Economics or closely related field required. Successful candidates must have demonstrated dedication to instruction and an ability to inspire students with his or her enthusiasm. Desired Qualifications We prefer candidates that have experience teaching the subject matter of the course and with teaching students that are at the level of the course (typically undergraduate students or masters students). Applicants may inquire about the specific courses that are being staffed at the time of their application. Required Application Materials Please submit the following: CV Cover letter List of references (names and emails only) Up to one optional document that could include statements about teaching, research interests, or contributions to diversity. Special Instructions All applicants must apply online at http://careers.msu.edu . Applications will be reviewed as needed. Website http://econ.msu.edu Department Statement The mission of the Department of Economics at Michigan State University consists of three interrelated components: providing the highest quality instruction to our undergraduate and graduate students, conducting leading-edge research in economics, and providing leadership and service to our professional communities. As a unit in a major land-grant university, we are committed to excel in all three components of our mission. MSU is committed to achieving excellence through cultural diversity. The university actively encourages applications and/or nominations from women, persons of color, veterans, and persons with disabilities. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. To learn more about the department, our faculty, and our undergraduate and graduate programs, please visit our website at http://econ.msu.edu. MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 36fe3d90 Last Name (required) 12beedce Email (required) cb1798fc Job Alert 23274fb2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Economics 10038238 Economics 10038238 Categories Area of Interest: Education/Training Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Area of Interest: Education/Training Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Social Science College Of Social Science By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the 