      "title": "Assistant Professor-FixedTerm",
      "description": "Assistant Professor-FixedTerm - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Assistant Professor-FixedTerm - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor-FixedTerm Physical Medicine And Rehabilitation 10034653 Faculty/Academic Staff Assistant Professor-FixedTerm East Lansing, Michigan, United States Physical Medicine And Rehabilitation 10034653 Area of Interest: Health Care Professional Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Aug 3 2026 Closing at: Aug 3 2028 - 23:55 EDT 100000.00 College Of Osteopathic Medicine 1148665 Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary PM&R Assistant Professor - Fixed Term. Responsibilities Include: Position will include clinical / outreach setting; teaching PMR Residents; and, research. Other general duties will include: Weekend call will include supervision of PM&R Residents on the inpatient floor, consults and possibly EMGs. Staffing consults on the inpatient floor and/or in a subacute rehab setting 2 half days per week with an average of 3-5 consults per half day. This will also include inpatient EMGs. Participation PM&R resident didactics to include approximately 4 presentations per year. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Terminal -Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Minimum Requirements Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine (DO) or Medical Doctor (MD).Candidates must be Board Certified or Eligible. Qualify for licensure in the State of Michigan. Required Application Materials Cover Letter CV Review of Applications Begins On 08/21/2026 Summary of Health Risks Exposure to human blood, serum, tissue and other bodily fluids; and materials covered under universal precautions. Website HTTPS://PMR.MSU.EDU/ Department Statement The mission of the Department of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation is to provide excellent clinical care, education, and research in the field of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation for the purpose of leading to optimum quality of life for individuals with physical disabilities. MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) e1300b17 Last Name (required) 5bd64047 Email (required) 2d80a7fc Job Alert 8d9fa6bd Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Physical Medicine And Rehabilitation 10034653 Physical Medicine And Rehabilitation 10034653 Categories Area of Interest: Health Care Professional Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Health Care Professional Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Osteopathic Medicine College Of Osteopathic Medicine By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related informat