    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/ast-asc-full-prof-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Ast/Asc/Full Prof-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Ast/Asc/Full Prof-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Ast/Asc/Full Prof-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Ast/Asc/Full Prof-Fixed Term Biomedical Laboratory Diagnostics Progr 10032580 Faculty/Academic Staff Ast/Asc/Full Prof-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Biomedical Laboratory Diagnostics Progr 10032580 Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Health Care Professional Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Jul 27 2026 Closing at: Jul 27 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Natural Science 1148542 Add to favorites View favorites Working/Functional Title Biomedical Laboratory Diag. Open Rank Professor Position Summary This is an exciting opportunity to educate future healthcare and research professionals and contribute to the growth and development of the medical laboratory profession. We value innovative teaching that is discipline-focused while promoting student personal growth, and we are committed to creating community and excellence for faculty, staff, and learners. Professional development in teaching and involvement in the laboratory profession will be valued. The Biomedical Laboratory Diagnostics Program at Michigan State University invites applications for two Fixed Term Faculty positions (non-tenure) at a rank commensurate with experience. The appointments will be academic year, nine-month positions. The initial appointment is for one year. Reappointment will be considered contingent on program needs, available funding, and satisfactory performance. The MSU fixed-term faculty system provides opportunities for advancement through the professorial ranks (Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, and Professor). Additionally, following seven semesters of exemplary performance, faculty members may be eligible to apply for Designation B status, which provides five-year, rolling appointments. These individuals will be responsible for in-person and online instruction at the undergraduate and graduate level. The teaching load will be approximately 3 courses per semester. Specific teaching assignments will be based on the successful candidate's areas of expertise and the instructional needs of the BLD program. Additional responsibilities may include a combination of service, outreach, and curriculum development, based on the individual’s expertise and interest. Professional engagement, such as involvement with medical laboratory-related professional societies, is strongly encouraged. The salary is negotiable and commensurate with experience. The Biomedical Laboratory Diagnostics (BLD) Program was established in 1926 and is within the College of Natural Science. MSU BLD offers two undergraduate degrees, Biomedical Laboratory Science and Medical Laboratory Science (a NACCLS accredited program) and three graduate degrees – an MA in Biomedical Laboratory Science, an MS in Clinical Laboratory Science, and an MS in Biomedical Laboratory Operations. Primary disciplines we teach include hematology and hemostasis, molecular diagnostics, scientific writing, laboratory management, pathology, clinical chemistry, immunology, immunohematology, and medical microbiology. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Biological sciences, public health, education, health sciences, or related field. Minimum Requirements A doctoral degree in biological sciences, public health, education, health sciences, or a related field. Hold a clinical certification/credential (such as MLS, MB, etc.) or be certification eligible. For more information on eligibility/routes to certification, click here: https://www.ascp.org/content/board-of-certification/get-credentialed# Hold a clinical certification/credential (such as MLS, MB, etc.) or be certification eligible. For more information on eligibility/routes to certification, click here: https://www.ascp.org/content/board-of-certification/get-credentialed# Demonstrated teaching ability as reflected in experiences educating or training people. Desired Qualifications Experience with discipline-based education research, scholarship of teaching and learning, and/or scholarly approaches to curriculum development. Evidence of working collaboratively in a team setting. Experience teaching in a relevant field as an instructor of record. Professional experience developing and/or disseminating knowledge in a relevant field through research, outreach, publication, or presentations. Participation in professional societies (such as ASCLS, ASCP, etc.). History of ongoing professional development. Work experience in the medical laboratory field Required Application Materials Cover letter (no more than 2 pages) that describes how your educational background and professional experience have prepared you to contribute to the BLD program as a teaching faculty member. If you possess any of the desired qualifications, please explain how those experiences have also prepared you for this position. CV Names and contact information of 3 professional references who will be contacted if invited for a final interview. Special Instructions Review of applications will begin 1 month from the posting date and will continue until the positions are filled. Questions regarding the position(s)s may be directed to Angela Wholehan, Teaching Specialist, BLD (angelalw@msu.edu). Job applications should be made through the MSU Careers website at https://careers.msu.edu . Posting number 1148542 . Review of Applications Begins On 08/27/2026 Summary of Health Risks Exposure to human blood, serum, tissue and other body fluids; and materials covered under Universal Precautions. Website https://bld.natsci.msu.edu/ Department Statement The Biomedical Laboratory Diagnostics (BLD) Program was established in1926 and is within the College of Natural Science. MSU BLD offers two undergraduate degrees, Biomedical Laboratory Science and Medical Laboratory Science (a NACCLS accredited program) and three graduate degrees – an MA in Biomedical Laboratory Science, an MS in Clinical Laboratory Science, and an MS in Biomedical Laboratory Operations. Primary disciplines we teach include hematology and hemostasis, molecular diagnostics, scientific writing, laboratory management, pathology, clinical chemistry, immunology, immunohematology, and medical microbiology. MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 870875b7 Last Name (required) f2237934 Email (required) d818f369 Job Alert be4d57d6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Biomedical Laboratory Diagnostics Progr 10032580 Biomedical Laboratory Diagnostics Progr 10032580 Categories Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Health Care Professional Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Health Care Professional Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Natural Science College Of Natural Science By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) 5562dd50 Last Name (required) 2c924658 Email (required) 3d11af6c Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Michigan State University is committed to safeguarding the privacy of personal data. To understand what type of information MSU Sites collects and how that information is used, view the MSU Privacy Statement . Visitors have the option of disabling or not accepting cookies by changing the preferences on their browser. If visitors disable cookies, they will still be able to use most sections of MSU Sites, but some sections may require the use of cookies. MSU also will not be able to tailor content to a visitor’s interests without cookies and a person will not be able to use any parts of MSU Sites that require a login. You consent to our cookies continue to browse this site. If you click on \"Accept essential only\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the My Profile link on the top right of the browser window. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a unit"
