    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-scholar-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-ff6a74ee-8c9c-481c-a696-881a7a633784": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term Ecology, Evolution And Behavior 10032245 Faculty/Academic Staff Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Ecology, Evolution And Behavior 10032245 Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Jul 27 2026 Closing at: Jul 27 2028 - 23:55 EDT 65000.00 College Of Natural Science 1149539 Add to favorites View favorites Working/Functional Title Presidential Postdoctoral Fellow Position Summary We encourage applications from candidates in any early career stage, from finishing Ph.D. students to current postdoctoral scholars. Current MSU EEB graduate students and postdocs are eligible to apply; however, they should make clear in their application materials how the proposed Presidential Postdoc research plan would represent a new direction for them. There are two main functions of this fellowship: RESEARCH PROGRAM: The Fellow will be a fully participating member of EEB at MSU and will be expected to have a cutting-edge research program that bridges the interests of two or more EEB core faculty members. A list of possible faculty members available to mentor the chosen candidate is available to review online . Candidates are required to contact potential faculty mentors before applying, as each faculty mentor will need to fill out a sponsor form for applicants to be considered. COMMUNITY ENGAGEMENT: The Fellow will also contribute to the EEB community via a community engagement initiative. The proposed initiative is up to the discretion of the applicant; possible ideas include (but are not limited to): a professional development workshop for current EEB grad students and postdocs; a co-working group; an EEB grad/postdoc-led working group that leads to a published outcome. The Fellows research stipend may also be used to support the community engagement initiative. The Fellow should consult with their prospective mentors during development of their proposed Community Engagement plan and they should explain in their application materials how their Community Engagement initiative would benefit the EEB community. Applicants are welcome to continue previous successful Community Engagement initiatives . The position is for two years, subject to review after one year, and will begin between June 1 and September 1, 2027. The role has a starting annual salary of $65,000 plus benefits, as well as a research stipend of $8,000 per year. Up to $1,000 of moving expenses may be reimbursed from the research stipend in the first year. A summary of available benefits to faculty, academic and support staff is available for applicants to review . For the most up to date information on the position, please visit the MSU EEB Website for more details . Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate Minimum Requirements Candidates will have completed a Ph.D. degree by the position start date. Candidates must have strong motivation for academic research. Desired Qualifications Candidates will be expected to propose a cutting-edge research programthat bridges the interests of two or more EEB core faculty members. They should have peer-review publications and demonstrate exceptional potential for research success in ecology, evolution, and/or behavior. Required Application Materials Applicants will need to enter the contact information for three references willing to write letters of recommendation on behalf of the candidate. MSU HR will contact references directly for selected applicants. Each faculty sponsor (not the applicant) should fill out the sponsorform to indicate their support for the candidate's application, how the candidate's research will integrate into the faculty members lab, anda brief description of the mentor's contributions to the EEB community (service, teaching, etc.). The required application materials for this role should be uploaded by the candidate as four separate attachments to the application: Cover letter (1 page max.) CV Other Document #1 Research statement including past research accomplishments and proposed research plans as an EEB postdoctoral fellow (2 pages max.) Community Engagement Proposal (1 page max.) Other Document #2 Up to two publications, preprints or manuscripts representative of the applicants work uploaded as a single file Special Instructions Review of applications will begin November 1, 2026. Please visit the MSU EEB Website for more details . Review of Applications Begins On 11/01/2026 Website HTTPS://EEB.MSU.EDU/ MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 42e3f96d Last Name (required) 6ada8371 Email (required) e262d008 Job Alert 88d98b08 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Ecology, Evolution And Behavior 10032245 Ecology, Evolution And Behavior 10032245 Categories A