    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-scholar-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-b07f88e8-314a-4c0d-90d3-17460d71759d": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term Plant Soil And Microbial Sciences 40000781 Faculty/Academic Staff Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Plant Soil And Microbial Sciences 40000781 Area of Interest: Agriculture Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Information Technology Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Jun 25 2026 Closing at: Jun 25 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Agriculture And Nat Resources 1143687 Position Summary The Kravchenko Lab in the Department of Plant, Soil, and Microbial Sciences at Michigan State University is seeking a Postdoctoral Scholar to conduct research focused on root characteristics of plants in annual and perennial cropping and native vegetation systems and their contribution as drivers of processes of soil carbon sequestration. The experimental component of the position will involve field soil and root sample collections from multiple experimental sites aimed at better understanding how different plant systems contribute to soil carbon accrual and weather variations in weather patterns (such as droughts and deluges) might influence it. . The project involves 13C plant labeling, root structure analysis, and X-ray computed micro-tomography. Job Duties: Travel to experimental sites as needed for deep core soil sampling. Analyses of root scans and measurements of soil properties. X-ray computed tomography scanning of soil samples and image analyses. Analyses of the collected data. Publication results in peer-reviewed journals and presentations at national/international conferences. Starting date is September 2026 or as soon as possible after that. The position is for one year with a possibility of a renewal contingent upon funding and satisfactory performance. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Soil Science or Ecology/Biology with interest in Soil Science or Related Minimum Requirements Ph. D. in Soil Science or Ecology/Biology with interest in Soil Science. In-depth knowledge of soil science and plant-soil interactions and advanced experience with X-ray computed tomography applications in soil science. A track record of publication in quality peer-review journals. Desired Qualifications Demonstrated creativity, independence, and excellent communication skills, both written and oral. Required Application Materials Cover Letter Resume/CV Name and contact information for Three (3) professional references An example of scientific work published in a peer-reviewed journal ( Optional ) Transcripts(unofficial) from past academic studies Special Instructions Applications should include a single pdf file that includes: 1) a cover letter (1-2 pages) highlighting how past experience and academic training align with the position, 2) a curriculum vitae including a list of all peer-reviewed publications and scientific presentations, 3) an example of scientific work published in a peer-reviewed journal, and 4) ( optional ) transcripts (unofficial) from the past academic studies. Inquiries regarding position can be sent to Dr. Alexandra Kravchenko ( kravche1@msu.edu ) Review of Applications Begins On 07/13/2026 Website https://www.canr.msu.edu/psm/ MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) e75e5a3a Last Name (required) eabfc785 Email (required) 8c669e30 Job Alert 0c33cc35 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Plant Soil And Microbial Sciences 40000781 Plant Soil And Microbial Sciences 40000781 Categories Area of Interest: Agriculture Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Information Technology Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Agriculture Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Information Technology Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Agriculture And Nat Resources College Of Agriculture And Nat Resources By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mg