    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/ast-asc-full-professor-health-program-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Ast/Asc/Full Professor Health Program Fixed Term",
      "description": "Ast/Asc/Full Professor Health Program Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Ast/Asc/Full Professor Health Program Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Ast/Asc/Full Professor Health Program Fixed Term Radiology Osteopathic Medicine 10034711 Faculty/Academic Staff Ast/Asc/Full Professor Health Program Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Radiology Osteopathic Medicine 10034711 Area of Interest: Health Care Professional Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Apr 9 2026 Closing at: Apr 9 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Osteopathic Medicine 1119388 Working/Functional Title Radiologist (Ast/Asc/Full Prof) Position Summary Join the dynamic team at Michigan State University Radiology as we seek board-certified or board-eligible radiologists in various subspecialties. We offer on-site and hybrid positions, fostering work-life balance while meeting patient needs. We are seeking individuals with experience providing high quality interpretation, who are passionate about cultivating a high-quality, patient-focused practice and are dedicated to excellence, embracing a collaborative peer-learning environment. Our radiologists interpret a wide range of diagnostic imaging studies, providing exceptional patient-centered care at our cutting-edge imaging centers, built in 2022 and 2023. Our facilities boast state-of-the-art MR, CT, PET/CT, ultrasound, and general diagnostic equipment. As a full-time faculty member in the Michigan State University Colleges of Osteopathic and Human Medicine Department of Radiology, you will have opportunities for academic advancement, mentorship, and leadership roles. Faculty are encouraged to participate in teaching residents and students, collaborate on research projects, and pursue scholarly activities that align with their interests. Benefits Competitive base salary plus signing bonus Additional income opportunities for shifts beyond 187 clinical shifts per year 22 vacation days, 15 holidays, and 21 non-clinical days offered to participate in administrative, teaching, and research opportunities MSU honors work and personal lives, providing a culture that supports work life balance, health, and wellbeing Limited evening and weekend duties Generous CME allowance, including up to 15 designated CME days Exceptional retirement matching program - MSU provides 10% match on employee's 5% contribution Additional 403(b) and 457(b) supplemental retirement accounts available Comprehensive health, dental, vision, life, and disability insurance offerings Tuition discounts of 50% for dependent children, spouses, and domestic partners MSU is a qualifying employer for the federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness program Michigan offers an affordable cost of living, with the mid-Michigan area providing a delightful mix of urban amenities and small-town charm, approximately one hour from both metro Detroit and Grand Rapids areas Enjoy numerous music and theatre offerings at the Wharton Center for the Performing Arts and the Broad Art Museum and exciting Big Ten Conference games at our exceptional sports venues Learn more about our community - MSU Radiology was recently featured on American Dream TV (ADTV): https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NbV460b7vKE Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Radiology Minimum Requirements MD, DO or equivalent Board-eligible or board-certified in Radiology Eligible for State of Michigan medical licensure Desired Qualifications Completed ACGME-accredited fellowship Additional certification in neuroradiology, interventional radiology or nuclear medicine (as applicable) Required Application Materials CV Cover letter Special Instructions As the hiring process moves forward, professional references will be required and contacted at a mutually agreed upon time. Review of Applications Begins On 05/15/2026 Summary of Health Risks Exposure to human blood, serum, tissue and other body fluids; and materials covered under Universal Precautions. TB risk or work within 3 feet of human patients in a health care setting or have potential exposure to animals or to specimens with Mycobacterium. Remote Work Statement MSU strives to provide a flexible work environment and this position has been designated as remote-friendly. Remote-friendly means some or all of the duties can be performed remotely as mutually agreed upon. Website https://radiology.msu.edu/ Department Statement At MSU Radiology, our mission is clear: we strive to provide extraordinary patient-centered care, fueled by world-class education and research that pioneers the transformation of diagnostic imaging through novel techniques and image-guided therapies. We are committed to investing in our most precious resource, human capital, providing an environment to build careers in a supportive culture of innovation and shared discovery. We are dedicated to pushing the boundaries of radiology, revolutionizing patient care, and driving breakthroughs that impact healthcare globally through our multidisciplinary research collaborations. Our clinical facilities include the state-of-the-art East Lansing Imaging Center, situated at the Izzo Family Medical Building on our McLaren Campus. This center opened in June 2023 and houses cutting-edge MR, CT, PET/CT, ultrasound, and general diagnostic equipment, enabling us to deliver precise and comprehensive imaging services to our patients. Our research infrastructure is expanding with a new PET/MR and translational imaging facility currently under construction. With this advanced technology, we aim to enhance access to imaging, patient comfort, diagnostic accuracy, and optimized treatment, leading to improved health outcomes. Our commitment to patient care extends beyond our university campus through strong partnerships with statewide community health providers. Collaborations with McLaren, Corewell Health, and Henry Ford Health System allow us to reach a broader patient base and contribute to the betterment of healthcare throughout Michigan. Additionally, we nurture strong academic-industry collaborations with imaging manufacturers, BAMF Health, and Cardinal Health. These partnerships enable us to access the latest advancements in medical technology and drive innovation in radiological imaging and therapies. Together, we work towards elevating the standard of care and ensuring our patients receive the best possible treatment options. MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 3f7bb07d Last Name (required) 8c57c8e5 Email (required) 742cfb22 Job Alert 2073eccd Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Radiology Osteopathic Medicine 10034711 Radiology Osteopathic Medicine 10034711 Categories Area of Interest: Health Care Professional Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Heal