      "description": "Ast Prof/Asc Prof/Prof - Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Ast Prof/Asc Prof/Prof - Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Ast Prof/Asc Prof/Prof - Fixed Term Agricultural Food And Resource Economics 10002036 Faculty/Academic Staff Ast Prof/Asc Prof/Prof - Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Agricultural Food And Resource Economics 10002036 Area of Interest: Agriculture Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Apr 15 2026 Closing at: Apr 15 2028 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Agriculture And Nat Resources 1122220 Working/Functional Title Ast Prof/Asc Prof/Prof - Fixed Term Position Summary The Department of Agricultural, Food, and Resource Economics (AFRE) seeks qualified candidates to work on multiple aspects of its research and activities under the Food Security Group (FSG). Appointments may support a range of funded projects and initiatives administered by AFRE/FSG. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -PhD in Agricultural Economics or closely related field Minimum Requirements PhD in Agricultural Economics or closely related field At least 5 years of experience conducting collaborative research with policy research centers in North America, Europe, Africa, Asia, or Latin America Demonstrated track record of peer review and other publishing with local collaborators Past experiences working with AFRE and FSG, either as a direct MSU employee or in close and extended collaboration with MSU/AFRE/FSG faculty Desired Qualifications Direct work experience with at least three North America, Europe, Africa, Asia, or Latin America research institutions that have recently partnered with MSU/AFRE/FSG in its work. At least 10 years of experience conducting collaborative research with policy research centers in North America, Europe, Africa, Asia, or Latin America Access to external funding to support appointment activities. Required Application Materials CV Cover letter Review of Applications Begins On 04/22/2026 Remote Work Statement MSU strives to provide a flexible work environment and this position has been designated as remote-friendly. Remote-friendly means some or all of the duties can be performed remotely as mutually agreed upon. Website https://www.canr.msu.edu/afre/ MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) f9259ace Last Name (required) 8c0de351 Email (required) 98b5d976 Job Alert 8254b09a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Agricultural Food And Resource Economics 10002036 Agricultural Food And Resource Economics 10002036 Categories Area of Interest: Agriculture Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Remote Work: Remote-Friendly Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Agriculture Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full