      "description": "Resident-On-Call - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Resident-On-Call - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Resident-On-Call Radiology Osteopathic Medicine 10034711 Faculty/Academic Staff Resident-On-Call East Lansing, Michigan, United States Radiology Osteopathic Medicine 10034711 Area of Interest: Health Care Professional Full Time/Part Time: On-Call Group: Faculty Academic Staff On-Call Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Mar 4 2026 Closing at: Mar 4 2028 - 23:55 EST Pay Commensurate with Experience College Of Osteopathic Medicine 1114317 Working/Functional Title Evening/Wknd Resident-Radiology Contrast Coverage Position Summary Variable shifts working in the Izzo Family Medicine Center in the Outpatient Imaging Department, including nights and weekend coverage, up to 10 hours per week. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate Minimum Requirements Licensed physician in the state of Michigan, with CS-3 Credentialed at McLaren Desired Qualifications Currently a resident physician at McLaren Required Application Materials CV Cover letter stating your availability Special Instructions Please indicate all availability for shifts that can be covered. Applications will be reviewed as needed. Work Hours Up to 10 hours per week, including nights and weekend coverage Summary of Health Risks Exposure to human blood, serum, tissue and other body fluids, and materials covered under Universal Precautions. Risks that have been identified by Environmental Health and Safety, such as exposure to lead, chemotherapy, formaldehyde, asbestos, and exposure to ionizing radiation and exposure to radiopharmaceuticals. Website radiology.msu.edu Department Statem