    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-scholar-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-29a53af2-043b-4316-a2df-1b7c24b51657": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term Biosystems And Agricultural Engineering 10002038 Faculty/Academic Staff Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Biosystems And Agricultural Engineering 10002038 Area of Interest: Agriculture Area of Interest: Engineers/Architects Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Feb 5 2026 Closing at: Feb 5 2028 - 23:55 EST Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Agriculture And Nat Resources 1110780 Position Summary We are seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Scholar to conduct research on the application of geophysical survey tools to quantify subsurface water dynamics and aquifer processes in irrigated agricultural systems. The successful candidate will integrate field-based geophysical measurements with hydrologic data and modeling approaches to improve understanding of water quantity, recharge, and subsurface flow in intensively managed fields. This position emphasizes the use of noninvasive geophysical methods to characterize spatial and temporal variability in soil moisture, vadose zone properties, shallow aquifer dynamics, and irrigation impacts on groundwater resources. Research Responsibilities Design and conduct geophysical surveys in irrigated fields using methods such as electrical resistivity tomography (ERT), electromagnetic induction (EMI), ground-penetrating radar (GPR), and related techniques Integrate geophysical data with hydrologic observations (e.g., soil moisture, groundwater levels, irrigation records, and precipitation) Analyze aquifer properties, recharge processes, and water quantity dynamics influenced by irrigation practices Develop and apply data processing workflows and inversion techniques for geophysical datasets Lead or contribute to peer-reviewed publications and technical reports Collaborate with interdisciplinary teams including hydrologists, agronomists, irrigation engineers, and extension specialists Support proposal development and reporting for externally funded projects This is a one year position from time of hire with the possibility of extension based off performance and funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Geophysics, Hydrogeology, Hydrology, Geological Engineering, Environmental Engineering, or a closely related field Minimum Requirements Experience with near-surface geophysical methods (ERT, EMI, GPR, seismic, or similar) Strong quantitative and data analysis skills Experience with field data collection in agricultural or environmental settings Demonstrated ability to publish in peer-reviewed journals Desired Qualifications Experience integrating geophysical data with groundwater or vadose zone models Familiarity with irrigation systems and agricultural water management Programming experience (e.g., Python, MATLAB, R) for data analysis and visualization Experience working in multidisciplinary research teams Required Application Materials C.V., cover letter, and contact information for three professional references. Special Instructions For more information, please contact Younsuk Dong at dongyoun@msu.edu . Review of Applications Begins On 02/09/2026 Summary of Physical Demands Lifting 30 pounds to waist level, 25 pounds to chest level. Carrying 30 pounds 30 feet Pushing/pulling 60 pound cart up to a maximum of 300 feet. Website https://www.canr.msu.edu/bae/ MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 4b441c07 Last Name (required) eb6f07e6 Email (required) 5d48d2b7 Job Alert 88e271ba Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Biosystems And Agricultural Engineering 10002038 Biosystems And Agricultural Engineering 10002038 Categories Area of Interest: Agriculture Area of Interest: Engineers/Architects Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Agriculture Area of Interest: Engineers/Architects Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Agriculture And Nat Resources College Of Agriculture And Nat Resources By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) 7346ebc5 Last Name (required) 1712f057 Email (required) 0ab9f6a6 Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Michigan State University is committed to safeguarding the privacy of personal data. To understand what type of information MSU Sites collects and how that information is used, view the MSU Privacy Statement . Visitors have the option of disabling or not accepting cookies by changing the preferences on their browser. If visitors disable cookies, they will still be able to use most sections of MSU Sites, but some sections may require the use of cookies. MSU also will not be able to tailor content to a visitor’s interests without cookies and a person will not be able to use any parts of MSU Sites that require a login. You consent to our cookies continue to browse this site. If you click on \"Accept essential only\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the My Profile link on the top right of the browser window. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a unit"
