    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-scholar-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-2bcde84b-73eb-4a02-9d03-94aaf840d9d2": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term Packaging 10002634 Faculty/Academic Staff Postdoctoral Scholar-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Packaging 10002634 Area of Interest: Engineers/Architects Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Jan 20 2026 Closing at: Jan 20 2028 - 23:55 EST Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Agriculture And Nat Resources 1107258 Position Summary 1. Conduct research tasks under the supervision of Dr. Joodaky (e.g. data collection, modeling, simulation). 2. Assist with analysis of materials and dynamics relevant to packaging. 3. Support ongoing research projects; may participate in modest independent sub-projects as time allows, always aligned with supervisor direction. 4. Operate and maintain lab equipment in packaging dynamics. 5. Assist in preparing results for publication / presentation; coauthoring as appropriate. 6. Attend the related internal and external (e.g. conferences) meetings and present the studies. 6. Expected to contribute to proposal writing if appropriate. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Mechanical, Civil Engineering, Material Science Minimum Requirements 1. A PhD in Mechanical, Civil, Materials, Aerospace Engineering (focus on solid mechanics, dynamics / vibrations). 2. Proficiency in Matlab and/or Python. 3. Experience in Finite Element Method modeling (Abaqus, Ansys) or similar. 4. Basic familiarity with machine learning (preferred). 5. Some record of research output (e.g. peer-reviewed papers, conference abstracts) or demonstrable research capability. Desired Qualifications 1. Familiarity with packaging structures (corrugated boards, polymer foams). 2. Knowledge of nonlinear dynamics, signal processing, composite mechanics, control theory and Energy Harvesting. 3. Hands-on lab experience: DIC, universal testers, accelerometers, shaker tables, vibration instrumentation. 4. Advanced/ deeper knowledge of machine learning. 5. Some exposure to fluid mechanics or multi-physics modeling. Required Application Materials A detailed CV including educational background, research experience, and publications. 2. A cover letter stating research interests, motivations for applying, and career aspirations. 3. Names and contact information for at least two academic references. Special Instructions The hiring unit reserves the right to reclassify or renegotiate terms if significant changes in duties or funding occur. Review of Applications Begins On 01/29/2026 Website www.packaging.msu.edu MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 7857a8b0 Last Name (required) 1dff9bc7 Email (required) bff8f50c Job Alert 3711848e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Packaging 10002634 Packaging 10002634 Categories Area of Inter