    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/research-associate-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-a4a0ff83-499b-4d34-9879-a2e231c287e2": {
      "title": "Research Associate-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Research Associate-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Research Associate-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Research Associate-Fixed Term Plant Research Laboratory Nat Science 10032674 Faculty/Academic Staff Research Associate-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Plant Research Laboratory Nat Science 10032674 Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Nov 20 2025 Closing at: Nov 20 2027 - 23:55 EST Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Natural Science 1097536 Position Summary The Dickson, Feig, Vermaas, Wei, Woldring laboratories together form Team Green, a collaborative research effort funded by DARPA to predict protein structural ensembles, ligand binding affinities, and protein functions through existing bioinformatics approaches and an extensive simulation campaign. To support these efforts, Team Green is looking for up to 4 qualified postdoctoral research associates to apply molecular simulation and mathematical methods to extend and develop these predictive tools into a broadly usable pipeline. Drs. Wei and Woldring will expect candidates with research experience and record in machine learning and deep learning modeling of biomolecular systems, structural and/or sequence bioinformatics. Research backgrounds in computational biophysics or mathematical AI are welcome. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Biophysics, Biochemistry, Physics, Computer Science, Mathematics, Chemical Engineering, or a related field Minimum Requirements Within the labs, we have our own unique strengths and requirements, but here are the minimum ones: A publication record commensurate with career stage and field Relevant prior research experience. This may be developing related AI/ML methods. or implementing, or running simulations at scale, depending on the group. Desired Qualifications Day to day, the expectation will depend on the research group a successful candidate is associated with. Drs. Dickson, Feig, and Vermaas will expect that the researcher has prior experience with a programming language such as python and Unix-based operating systems such as MacOS or Linux. These tools are essential to set up, carry out, and analyze molecular simulation trajectories, and to interact with high performance computing environments needed to run those trajectories. Thus, previous experience with these tools is beneficial but not essential: • Python libraries like Numpy, Scipy, Pandas, Pytorch, or Matplotlib • A programmable molecular viewer such as VMD • Simulation engines such as NAMD, CHARMM, OpenMM, AMBER, or GROMACS • Basic familiarity with the linux terminal Required Application Materials To best evaluate candidates, please provide a list of three recommenders so that the team can reach out when you advance to that stage. Review of Applications Begins On 12/01/2025 Website https://prl.natsci.msu.edu/ MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 2dee5cef Last Name (required) 225c5b51 Email (required) e5cc60c1 Job Alert 8eca03fb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Plant Research Laboratory Nat Science 10032674 Plant Research Laboratory Nat Science 10032674 Categories Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Natural Science College Of Natural Science By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) b5b0e8b1 Last Name (required) 01baa290 Email (required) fdb6bd41 Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Michigan State University is committed to safeguarding the privacy of personal data. To understand what type of information MSU Sites collects and how that information is used, view the MSU Privacy Statement . Visitors have the option of disabling or not accepting cookies by changing the preferences on their browser. If visitors disable cookies, they will still be able to use most sections of MSU Sites, but some sections may require the use of cookies. MSU also will not be able to tailor content to a visitor’s interests without cookies and a person will not be able to use any parts of MSU Sites that require a login. You consent to our cookies continue to browse this site. If you click on \"Accept essential only\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the My Profile link on the top right of the browser window. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a unit"
