    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/assist-assoc-professor-health-programs-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-251117c8-e372-4eca-9f8e-47251d364093": {
      "title": "Assist/Assoc Professor Health Programs Fixed Term",
      "description": "Assist/Assoc Professor Health Programs Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Assist/Assoc Professor Health Programs Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Assist/Assoc Professor Health Programs Fixed Term Medicine 10022582 Faculty/Academic Staff Assist/Assoc Professor Health Programs Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Medicine 10022582 Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Jul 28 2025 Closing at: Jul 28 2027 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Human Medicine 1059652 Working/Functional Title Assist/Assoc Professor Health Programs Fixed Term Position Summary The Department of Medicine at Michigan State University, Division of Hematology and Oncology, is seeking an MD/DO for a clinical position at the rank of Assistant/Associate Professor level in the Health Programs (HP) faculty track. This is a clinical faculty position with responsibilities that include direct patient care and active engagement in the education of medical students, residents, and hematology/oncology fellows. In addition to clinical and teaching duties, the successful candidate is expected to participate in translational/clinical trials and collaborate with other medical oncologists, surgeons, radiation oncologists, and basic scientists. Michigan State University has an expanding community-based medical school and a growing hematology/oncology clinical and translational research division. As a founding member of the NSABP and a member of SWOG, our active clinical trials program includes cooperative group, industry-supported, and investigator-initiated trials. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -M.D. or D.O. Minimum Requirements Must possess a Michigan Medical license, Board of Pharmacy and DEA licenses. Physicians must be Board certified in Hematology and or Oncology. Board eligible candidates are expected to obtain board certification in Hematology and/or Oncology within one year of the hire date. Required Application Materials CV and Cover Letter Special Instructions Applications will be accepted until a suitable candidate is identified. If you have any questions, please contact Jatin Rana, M.D. Division of Hematology/Oncology, by email at ranajat1@msu.edu. Review of Applications Begins On 08/05/2025 Summary of Health Risks Exposure to human blood, serum, tissue, and other body fluids, and materials covered under Universal Precautions. TB risk or work within 3 feet of human patients in a health care setting. Website https://medicine.chm.msu.edu/ MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) e8b9df51 Last Name (required) 794410e0 Email (required) cd65cf9a Job Alert 712c424b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Medicine 10022582 Medicine 10022582 Categories Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Human Medicine College Of Human Medicine By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) 963fb5db Last Name (required) 837bd40d Email (required) 519558d2 Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Michigan State University is committed to safeguarding the privacy of personal data. To understand what type of information MSU Sites collects and how that information is used, view the MSU Privacy Statement . Visitors have the option of disabling or not accepting cookies by changing the preferences on their browser. If visitors disable cookies, they will still be able to use most sections of MSU Sites, but some sections may require the use of cookies. MSU also will not be able to tailor content to a visitor’s interests without cookies and a person will not be able to use any parts of MSU Sites that require a login. You consent to