    "https://careers.msu.edu/jobs/instructor-fixed-term-east-lansing-michigan-united-states-4adb3628-aad2-49f6-9b0b-4747429f7518": {
      "title": "Instructor-Fixed Term",
      "description": "Instructor-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Instructor-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Instructor-Fixed Term Physics-Astronomy 10032666 Faculty/Academic Staff Instructor-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Physics-Astronomy 10032666 Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Part Time (1-49.9%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Jul 1 2025 Closing at: Jul 1 2027 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Natural Science 1056229 Position Summary The Department of Physics and Astronomy at Michigan State University (MSU) invites applications for a fixed-term position as an instructor in physics. The central responsibility of this position will be to teach upper-division lab courses, including electronics and optics. A PhD in physics or related field at the time of the start of the position is required, and previous experience teaching upper-division lab courses is required. The appointment will be for the 2025-2026 academic year; the salary will be based on experience. The appointment is potentially renewable for additional years based on department needs and satisfactory performance. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Masters -Physics or related field Desired Degree Doctorate -Physics or related field Minimum Requirements A Masters degree in physics or related field at the time of the start of the position is required, and previous experience teaching upper-division lab courses is required. Desired Qualifications A Ph.D. in physics or related field at the time of the start of the position is preferred Required Application Materials Applications should be submitted through the MSU hiring website (http://careers.msu.edu). Applicants should include: (1) a cover letter; (2) a CV including teaching experience; (3) a one-page statement of teaching experience and philosophy; (4) a one-page statement of your experience fostering diversity, equity, and inclusion in previous professional settings, and how you plan to contribute in these areas at MSU as part of this position; and (5) the names and contact information for three references, who may be contacted. Please include all information in a single PDF file. Special Instructions Review of applications will begin on July 8, 2025, and will continue until the position is filled; all applications received by this date will receive full consideration. Questions may be directed to Stuart Tessmer ( tessmer@msu.edu ). Review of Applications Begins On 07/08/2025 Website https://pa.msu.edu/ MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) da30aba2 Last Name (required) 9357e996 Email (required) 161187a1 Job Alert d05cbfaf Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Physics-Astronomy 10032666 Physics-Astronomy 10032666 Categories Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Part Time (1-49.9%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Part Time (1-49.9%) Group: Fixed Term Faculty Union/Non-Union: Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Natural Science College Of Natural Science By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-depth experience with the SIS system (student.msu.edu) and the University’s Admissions platform (Slate). [Bidding eligibility ends October 20, 2026, 11:55 PM] Senior Production Manager / Stage Manager East Lansing Performing Arts Facilities & Programs 10052643 Wharton Center for Performing Arts seeks an organized, collaborative Senior Production Manager to help bring live performances and events to the stage. Working closely with the Technical Director, this position coordinates technical production for touring attractions, performances, rehearsals, rentals, and special programs. (The Bidding Eligibility ends on 10/20/2026 at 11:55 PM) Already applied? Click here Apply Now First Name (required) d0fb1e9b Last Name (required) 514f221c Email (required) 89ad7e1b Refer someone to this job By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Michigan State University is committed to safeguarding the privacy of personal data. To understand what type of information MSU Sites collects and how that information is used, view the MSU Privacy Statement . Visitors have the option of disabling or not accepting cookies by changing the preferences on their browser. If visitors disable cookies, they will still be able to use most sections of MSU Sites, but some sections may require the use of cookies. MSU also will not be able to tailor content to a visitor’s interests without cookies and a person will not be able to use any parts of MSU Sites that require a login. You consent to our cookies continue to browse this site. If you