      "title": "Assistant Professor-On-Call",
      "description": "Assistant Professor-On-Call - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Assistant Professor-On-Call - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor-On-Call Pa Medicine 40001090 Faculty/Academic Staff Assistant Professor-On-Call East Lansing, Michigan, United States Pa Medicine 40001090 Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Health Care Professional Full Time/Part Time: On-Call Group: Faculty Academic Staff On-Call Union/Non-Union: Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Mar 28 2025 Closing at: Mar 28 2027 - 23:55 EDT Pay Commensurate with Experience College Of Osteopathic Medicine 1030105 Position Summary PA Medicine is in search of additional faculty help in the Physical Examination and Procedures and Diagnostics courses (which occur each semester, from semesters 1-4). These courses contain physical exam and procedural skills labs and check offs, and other simulated events, which require additional instructors to assist principal faculty to properly run and/or grade the events. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -PA-C Minimum Requirements Required Qualifications: Master’s degree in physician assistant studies from an accredited program Current NCCPA Certification A valid physician assistant license for the State of Michigan or eligibility to obtain such licensure. OR Doctoral degree, DO or MD with active Board certification and state licensure in Michigan or eligibility to obtain such licensure. Desired Qualifications Strong interpersonal abilities with excellent verbal and written communication skills to effectively communicate with students, staff, faculty, administrators, and the public. Familiarity with the use of computers for organization, word processing, and communication. Enthusiastic about working in a collaborative environment. Self-motivated with refined organizational skills. Required Application Materials CV Cover Letter Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion (DEI) statement. Submit a description of your past experiences and contributions to inclusive excellence including a brief description of your ideas for future initiatives that you would like to implement to support MSUCOM's commitment to inclusive excellence. https://osteopathicmedicine.msu.edu/about-us/diversity-inclusion-safety Special Instructions N/A Work Hours Between 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Review of Applications Begins On 04/11/2025 Website pa.com.msu.edu MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 8b48316f Last Name (required) d6f5f369 Email (required) b0cf6a38 Job Alert 2a879404 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Pa Medicine 40001090 Pa Medicine 40001090 Categories Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Health Care Professional Full Time/Part Time: On-Call Group: Faculty Academic Staff On-Call Union/Non-Union: Union Area of Interest: Education/Training Area of Interest: Health Care Professional Full Time/Part Time: On-Call Group: Faculty Academic Staff On-Call Union/Non-Union: Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Osteopathic Medicine College Of Osteopathic Medicine By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In Other Jobs At MSU? Check out these other recently posted roles that might be right for you! Executive Mgtmt Director-Exec Mgt East Lansing Msu It Campus It Experience 40000843 Join MSU IT where you’ll have the opportunity to influence enterprise-wide IT services at a leading public research university, shape the future of campus technology experiences, and lead teams that make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the broader MSU community. Professional Aide Project Pay East Lansing Music 10030598 The College of Music offers an opportunity for classical musicians who are seeking to accompany other musicians and entertain our audiences with professional and thrilling performances Assistant/Associate Professor Tenure System East Lansing Psychology Social Science 10038698 The Department of Psychology at Michigan State University is recruiting a faculty member with expertise in industrial and organizational psychology or a related field for a tenure system appointment at the assistant or associate professor level starting Fall 2027. Herder I East Lansing Campus Livestock Centers Canr 40001114 This is a temporary position. MSU Dairy Teaching and Research Center is looking for an someone to assist with daily chores associated with caring for a large herd of livestock. Academic Program Coordinator East Lansing Graduate School Dean 10067378 The Graduate School is looking for a professional with in-dep