      "description": "Research Associate-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Research Associate-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Research Associate-Fixed Term Computational Math Sci And Engr Egr 40000839 Faculty/Academic Staff Research Associate-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Computational Math Sci And Engr Egr 40000839 Area of Interest: Engineers/Architects Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Oct 18 2024 Closing at: Oct 18 2026 - 23:55 EDT Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Engineering 997212 Position Summary The successful candidate will hold a PhD in Physics, Mathematics, Computer Science, or related field, and will have significant research interests and demonstrated success in quantum information science. The candidate will work with Ryan LaRose in the Department Computational Mathematics, Science, and Engineering (CMSE) , with opportunities to collaborate with other faculty in the Center for Quantum Computing, Science, and Engineering (MSU-Q) . The start date for this position is flexible and applications will be reviewed until filled. The position is for one year with the opportunity to renew upon successful progress. Interested candidates are encouraged to contact Ryan LaRose ( rmlarose@msu.edu ). Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -Physics, Mathematics, Computer Science or related field Minimum Requirements PhD in Physics, Computer Science, Mathematics, or related field Dissertation topic and/or demonstrated research experience in quantum information science Desired Qualifications Strong familiarity with the mathematics of quantum information theory Experience in one or more of the following areas: Developing quantum algorithms and estimating their resources Classically simulating quantum circuits, with and without noise Developing and benchmarking quantum error mitigation techniques Designing quantum error correction codes and/or decoders for quantum error correction Experience with Python programming Experience with high-performance computing Experience with machine learning (theory and/or practice) Required Application Materials CV, Statement of research experience, interests, and proposal for future research (max 2 pages) Two letters of recommendation Review of Applications Begins On 11/11/2024 Website cmse.msu.edu MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) 33f3103c Last Name (required) 5ea1a550 Email (required) 0d46b02d Job Alert a23f2e61 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Computational Math Sci And Engr Egr 40000839 Computational Math Sci And Engr Egr 40000839 Categories Area of Interest: Engineers/Architects Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Engineers/Architects Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: 