      "description": "Research Associate-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Research Associate-Fixed Term - East Lansing, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Research Associate-Fixed Term Physics-Astronomy 10032666 Faculty/Academic Staff Research Associate-Fixed Term East Lansing, Michigan, United States Physics-Astronomy 10032666 Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Show More Show Less Faculty/Academic Staff Opening on: Nov 4 2024 Closing at: Nov 4 2026 - 23:55 EST Salary Commensurate with Experience College Of Natural Science 1000864 Position Summary The Lapidus and Feig labs at Michigan State University have an open Research Associate (postdoctoral) position for interdisciplinary research on protein interactions in a cellular environment. The position is primarily experimental but will also use computation to characterize the effects of crowding on biomolecular dynamics, stability, and diffusive properties. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, age, disability or protected veteran status. Required Degree Doctorate -physics, biophysics, biochemistry or related field Minimum Requirements Candidates should have a PhD in physics, biophysics, biochemistry or related field and experience in one or more of the following: optical spectroscopy, molecular biology and computational biology and an enthusiasm to learn new skills. Required Application Materials Interested applicants can apply for this job at http://careers.msu.edu position #### and include a cover letter, CV, and the contact information for 3 referees. Special Instructions More information about the labs can be found at the Lisa J Lapidus website and https://feig.bch.msu.edu/ . Review of the applications will begin on November 15, 2024 and continue until the position is filled. Contact Lisa Lapidus at lapidus@msu.edu with any questions about the position. Review of Applications Begins On 11/15/2024 MSU Statement Michigan State University has been advancing the common good with uncommon will for more than 160 years. One of the top research universities in the world, MSU pushes the boundaries of discovery and forges enduring partnerships to solve the most pressing global challenges while providing life-changing opportunities to a diverse and inclusive academic community through more than 200 programs of study in 17 degree-granting colleges. Apply Now Not Quite What You're Looking For? Sign Up For Job Alerts First Name (required) f474b4c9 Last Name (required) 6aefde0f Email (required) 3ca031d2 Job Alert 5831170b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Physics-Astronomy 10032666 Physics-Astronomy 10032666 Categories Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Area of Interest: Research/Scientific Full Time/Part Time: Full Time (90-100%) Group: Fixed Term Academic Staff Union/Non-Union: Non-Union Employment Type Faculty/Academic Staff Faculty/Academic Staff Locations East Lansing, Michigan, United States East Lansing, Michigan, United States Unit College Of Natural Science College Of Natural Science By clicking Send, you acknowledge that you are willing to receive SMS messages from Michigan State relating to the status of your application or other recruitment related information to any mobile / cell phone number entered in the form above. You can easily opt-out of receiving SMS messages by replying STOP to any messages you receive. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Interested In 